WEBVTT

00:05.092 --> 00:08.551
[Man On Phone]
I felt like I had a lot of time.

00:08.625 --> 00:10.992
[Woman ]
I know.

00:11.059 --> 00:15.053
It's good. I'm good.

00:15.126 --> 00:18.585
Yeah. We're, um- we're
just getting off the freeway.

00:18.659 --> 00:20.150
Yeah?

00:20.226 --> 00:22.718
Did, uh, Hugh pick you up at the office, or-

00:22.792 --> 00:25.227
Yeah, he was coming in from Oakland.

00:25.293 --> 00:28.889
He was late, of course. Then I took him-

00:28.959 --> 00:33.294
And then, uh, he took me to some lawyer bar.

00:33.359 --> 00:35.089
A lawyer bar?

00:35.159 --> 00:37.822
Yeah. A lawyer bar, kind of.

00:37.892 --> 00:41.260
Yeah. I don't know.
Everybody there seemed like a lawyer.

00:41.326 --> 00:43.454
I felt like I was the only person without a tie.

00:43.525 --> 00:47.018
Well, maybe we should get you
a tie for emergencies.

00:47.092 --> 00:48.583
Yeah, wardrobe emergencies.

00:48.659 --> 00:50.150
Yeah.

00:50.226 --> 00:54.129
Anyhow, we tried to take the freeway and-

00:55.026 --> 00:57.621
Ke- Kevin?

00:57.692 --> 01:00.184
I can barely hear you.

01:00.259 --> 01:02.592
Is that better?

01:02.659 --> 01:04.787
Not much.

01:04.859 --> 01:07.624
Where are you? Are you there yet?

01:07.692 --> 01:12.790
Yeah, I- I'm just pulling up right now.

01:12.859 --> 01:15.419
I just got here. Um-

01:17.393 --> 01:19.521
Yeah. I'm right here.

01:19.592 --> 01:23.825
I-You know what? I need to parallel park
and I'm not on my earpiece.

01:23.892 --> 01:25.622
Okay.

01:25.692 --> 01:27.854
Are you good?

01:27.926 --> 01:29.519
Yeah.

01:29.592 --> 01:31.686
You know, we should talk about,
you know-

01:31.759 --> 01:33.557
Maybe we can talk about, you know...

01:33.625 --> 01:36.390
that little problem before
we get into the party.

01:36.459 --> 01:38.451
Okay.

01:38.525 --> 01:41.154
Is it something we should talk about now, or-

01:42.826 --> 01:44.658
Hello?

01:44.725 --> 01:46.557
Kevin?

01:46.625 --> 01:48.719
I lost you.

01:48.792 --> 01:50.283
Oh.

01:50.359 --> 01:51.691
Baby?

01:51.759 --> 01:53.250
[Glass Shatters]

01:56.359 --> 01:58.624
You gotta be kidding me.

02:00.792 --> 02:03.057
I think olive oil would be good.
A little more maybe?

02:03.126 --> 02:04.617
- [Woman ] A drizzle.
- A little more.

02:04.692 --> 02:06.183
- Is this turning you on?
- That is hot.

02:06.259 --> 02:07.591
[ Laughs]

02:07.659 --> 02:09.594
[Woman ]
See how you're slipping? This is-

02:09.659 --> 02:12.254
- It's- It's the bread, babe.
- It's the two of you with the knives that-

02:12.326 --> 02:14.261
I have not had carbs for a week.

02:14.326 --> 02:16.022
I've been on this-this "cleanse."

02:16.092 --> 02:18.288
How long have you been cleansing for?

02:18.359 --> 02:20.123
About 21 days.

02:20.193 --> 02:22.856
I had my juice and my smoothie
earlier today...

02:22.926 --> 02:25.191
and I do feel very,
you know- [Sniffs]

02:25.259 --> 02:28.058
- Cleansed? Open?
- A little faint maybe?

02:28.126 --> 02:29.754
- [ Doorbell Rings]
- But I'm gonna eat...

02:29.826 --> 02:31.522
I'm gonna drink and have a good time.

02:31.592 --> 02:33.458
- [ Door Closes]
- Hi.

02:33.525 --> 02:35.016
- Hey.
- How are you guys?

02:35.092 --> 02:37.254
Nice to see you.

02:37.326 --> 02:39.591
- Bend down to my level, please.
- I know.

02:39.659 --> 02:42.561
So, I just had Kevin
on the phone and this happened.

02:42.625 --> 02:44.253
It cracked.

02:44.326 --> 02:45.817
As I was talking to him.

02:45.892 --> 02:47.758
- You dropped it.
- Our connection- No, I didn't drop it.

02:47.826 --> 02:49.624
It just cracked as I was holding it.

02:49.692 --> 02:51.524
Do you have insurance?

02:51.592 --> 02:53.288
I- I actually don't know if I do.

02:53.359 --> 02:55.555
Do you have the Skype app I showed you?

02:55.625 --> 02:58.493
No, I think it's fine. He just said he wanted
to talk about something...

02:58.559 --> 03:01.028
But on the news, you know,
they're talking about the comet.

03:01.092 --> 03:02.583
- Yeah.
- The Miller's Comet.

03:02.659 --> 03:05.527
And they keep telling people
that this can happen.

03:05.592 --> 03:07.083
Yeah. I don't think it's the comet.

03:07.159 --> 03:09.128
If you have Skype, it uses the home Wi-Fi.

03:09.193 --> 03:12.254
No. The interference.
They're saying things break.

03:12.326 --> 03:14.295
Hey, do you want some wine?

03:18.592 --> 03:21.756
Did Amir mention to you that...

03:21.826 --> 03:24.489
he's bringing Laurie...

03:24.559 --> 03:26.187
to dinner?

03:26.992 --> 03:28.483
He's bringing Laurie?

03:28.559 --> 03:30.858
Yeah. The Laurie.

03:30.926 --> 03:34.693
Um, no, I didn't know that. I didn't know that.

03:34.759 --> 03:36.250
- Who's Laurie?
- Well, he is.

03:36.326 --> 03:39.990
- You know Laurie.
- Oh, Mike.

03:40.059 --> 03:45.020
Long black hair. Kind of vixeny.

03:45.092 --> 03:47.220
Wild and sexy.

03:47.293 --> 03:49.819
- Oh.
- Kinda strange, very mysterious.

03:49.892 --> 03:52.225
- Very tight, tight, tight dresses.
- Listen.

03:52.293 --> 03:54.922
It's totally fine.
It's such an Amir thing to do.

03:54.992 --> 03:56.483
I was going to keep this-

03:56.559 --> 03:58.653
This, my friends.

03:58.725 --> 04:02.628
It's my own little rescue remedy concoction.

04:02.692 --> 04:05.127
- Right.
- It's our own mix.

04:05.193 --> 04:07.856
- It's pretty s- It's very safe, I think.
- Do you want a needle for that?

04:07.926 --> 04:10.225
- Is it clean?
- You can drop it into some water.

04:10.293 --> 04:12.262
Just take the edge off, in case you're worried.

04:12.326 --> 04:14.227
I don't know. I'm just- I'm offering.

04:14.293 --> 04:16.853
It's echinacea,
passion flower, a little Valerian...

04:16.926 --> 04:18.360
and ketamine.

04:18.426 --> 04:20.657
- So it's all natural.
- Ketamine?

04:20.725 --> 04:23.217
That doesn't sound natural at all.
That's a horse tranquilizer.

04:23.293 --> 04:25.728
- Yeah, but it's just a whisper of ketamine.
- I did that once.

04:25.792 --> 04:27.624
I just thought maybe a celebration-

04:27.692 --> 04:29.923
Are you offering this to me,
because Laurie's coming here?

04:29.992 --> 04:31.483
Well, I'm just saying-

04:31.559 --> 04:34.586
- Now it's a party.
- Ketamine or cheese?

04:34.659 --> 04:37.527
It's right here if you change your mind.
Oh, this is nice.

04:37.592 --> 04:38.992
Where'd you get this?

04:39.059 --> 04:40.550
- [ Doorbell Rings]
- Galaxy, that thrift store.

04:40.625 --> 04:42.856
- Oh, I love that place.
- Me too. I know.

04:42.926 --> 04:44.417
Oh. Hi.

04:44.492 --> 04:45.983
- Hi, baby.
- What?

04:46.059 --> 04:49.086
- Come on. Come here.
- All right.

04:49.159 --> 04:50.650
My wife.

04:50.725 --> 04:52.591
- Hi.
- Hey.

04:53.926 --> 04:55.724
- How are you?
- Hi. I'm good.

04:55.792 --> 04:57.454
- Hi.
- Hi.

04:57.525 --> 05:00.017
- Do you guys want wine?
- I do.

05:00.092 --> 05:01.651
Cheese? Ketamine?

05:03.059 --> 05:04.687
You look so good in leather.

05:04.759 --> 05:07.524
Jesus Christ.

05:07.592 --> 05:09.424
- Um-
- I want water or something.

05:13.326 --> 05:14.817
Did you know that, um...

05:14.892 --> 05:17.361
- Laurie is coming?
- There you go.

05:17.426 --> 05:19.918
Uh, no.

05:19.992 --> 05:21.654
- Laurie's coming?
- Yeah.

05:21.725 --> 05:23.387
Look at the smile on your face.

05:23.459 --> 05:26.190
- It's not a smile. It's not that smile.
- Oh. my God.

05:26.259 --> 05:28.592
- Why is she coming tonight?
- Amir's bringing her.

05:28.659 --> 05:31.254
Beats me, because Amir's a total jackass.

05:31.326 --> 05:32.487
Oh.

05:32.559 --> 05:35.222
You know what?
Put a quarter into the swear jar.

05:35.293 --> 05:37.091
So, who did he tell?

05:37.159 --> 05:39.060
Well, we got the-Yeah.

05:39.126 --> 05:41.254
We got an e-mail about it. Just his plus one.

05:41.326 --> 05:44.854
Plus one and then I was, like, plus what?

05:49.293 --> 05:51.489
- I need to know tonight?
- Mm-hmm.

05:51.559 --> 05:55.052
My editor needs to know how
to book hotels and flights.

05:55.126 --> 05:56.890
I gotta do it. Let them know.

05:59.592 --> 06:01.527
Gotta know tonight.

06:04.559 --> 06:06.425
You know I-I- I can't-

06:06.492 --> 06:07.983
I-I just need to think about it...

06:08.059 --> 06:09.994
a little bit longer because...

06:10.059 --> 06:11.652
I just don't want to make
the wrong choice.

06:11.725 --> 06:13.216
What if you came for a shorter time?

06:13.293 --> 06:16.058
Like a month, not the full four months.
Just come for a month.

06:16.992 --> 06:18.654
It's still a very long time...

06:18.725 --> 06:20.250
and I'm not saying no.

06:20.326 --> 06:24.764
Babe, if you don't say yes, it becomes a no.

06:25.625 --> 06:27.423
[ Doorbell Rings]

06:27.492 --> 06:29.586
We're cold and hungry.

06:29.659 --> 06:31.491
Hello?

06:31.559 --> 06:33.425
- Hello.
- Hi.

06:33.492 --> 06:36.121
- Amir, you look great.
- Thank you.

06:36.193 --> 06:37.718
- Hi.
- You remember Laurie?

06:37.792 --> 06:39.761
Amir told me I wouldn't be...

06:39.826 --> 06:41.920
- overdressed, now I'm feeling-
- No. No, no.

06:45.426 --> 06:47.019
- Hi.
- Hi.

06:47.092 --> 06:48.651
- How are you?
- I'm good.

06:48.725 --> 06:50.387
- Beth, do you remember Laurie?
- Yes.

06:50.459 --> 06:53.054
- Nice to see you.
- You guys already said hello and-

06:53.126 --> 06:54.685
How are you? Good to see you.

06:54.759 --> 06:57.024
You guys want red wine?

06:57.092 --> 06:59.652
Yes. I would love red wine.

06:59.725 --> 07:02.194
- Lee?
- I've been cooking. I've been cooking.

07:02.259 --> 07:04.728
- How have you been?
- I've been good. I've been really good.

07:04.792 --> 07:06.852
- You?
- I've been great.

07:06.926 --> 07:10.363
Yeah. Life is looking very different from
how it was a while back.

07:10.426 --> 07:13.021
- In a good way, so-
- Well, cool. That's good to hear.

07:13.092 --> 07:16.494
- I would hope so. There you go.
- Thank you.

07:18.092 --> 07:19.720
Not A, C, E.

07:19.792 --> 07:21.317
"Horace, listen.

07:21.393 --> 07:24.022
I'll be down at the pyramid.
Come on down and join.

07:24.092 --> 07:26.084
We gotta talk about some deity stuff."

07:26.159 --> 07:28.253
Does everyone else still not have service?

07:28.326 --> 07:30.852
My phone is completely broken.

07:30.926 --> 07:34.226
I'm living in the moment, but-

07:34.293 --> 07:36.489
- Nothing.
- I got zero.

07:36.559 --> 07:39.222
That's weird. Maybe the tower's down.

07:39.293 --> 07:41.262
The tower's down?

07:41.326 --> 07:43.261
I'm telling you guys-

07:43.326 --> 07:45.386
- It's not down.
- That would be a big news story.

07:45.459 --> 07:48.361
Comet. Comet.

07:48.426 --> 07:51.260
- Miller's Comet.
- Yes. Thank you.

07:51.326 --> 07:55.957
I read something this morning
about a comet in the 1930s.

07:56.026 --> 07:57.517
It was in Finland.

07:57.592 --> 07:59.424
- Knocked out all of the-
- I actually-

07:59.492 --> 08:01.723
the cell towers?

08:01.792 --> 08:05.160
Actually, it was in 1923.

08:05.226 --> 08:06.717
And, yes, it was in Finland.

08:06.792 --> 08:10.354
- Um-
- Thank you, Wikipedia.

08:10.426 --> 08:13.157
It was actually crazy,
because it affected the people.

08:13.226 --> 08:16.526
After it passed, they would get lost.

08:16.592 --> 08:18.891
They would end up in the wrong home.
They would forget things.

08:18.959 --> 08:20.928
They wouldn't really know where they were.

08:20.992 --> 08:23.552
And I remember reading about
this one woman...

08:23.625 --> 08:26.026
who called the police and said...

08:26.092 --> 08:28.186
"The man in my house is not my husband."

08:29.193 --> 08:30.684
And then police came over...

08:30.759 --> 08:33.160
and they said, "This is your husband"...

08:33.226 --> 08:34.922
And she said, "No. This is not my husband.

08:34.992 --> 08:37.086
- I killed my husband yesterday.
- Awesome.

08:37.159 --> 08:38.855
That's how I know it's not him."

08:38.926 --> 08:41.486
But they couldn't arrest her,
because he was standing...

08:41.559 --> 08:43.152
right there in front in them.

08:43.226 --> 08:45.161
Do they have any theories of why?

08:45.226 --> 08:48.526
Think how lucky she is.
She gets to kill him again.

08:48.592 --> 08:50.083
Clearly she wants to kill this man.

08:50.159 --> 08:51.650
- It's just the Finnish.
- The Finns.

08:51.725 --> 08:53.694
The Finns or Finnish?

08:53.759 --> 08:56.194
- You guys remember Halley's Comet?
- Yes.

08:56.259 --> 08:57.818
I mean, it was such a big deal.

08:57.892 --> 09:01.488
I remember at my school,
we all had to, like, reenact Halley's Comet.

09:01.559 --> 09:05.326
So, they assigned each of us
something celestial to do.

09:05.393 --> 09:07.919
My sister got to be Halley's Comet.
I was very jealous.

09:07.992 --> 09:10.587
I've never met your sister.
Have you guys met her sister?

09:10.659 --> 09:12.992
There's a picture of her right
over there on the mantel, but...

09:13.059 --> 09:15.426
- She's only a fleeting comet.
- she looks a little ridiculous.

09:15.492 --> 09:17.256
- That's your sister?
- But why did you put it-

09:17.326 --> 09:18.851
It's the door to nowhere.

09:18.926 --> 09:20.861
In feng shui, a useless door...

09:20.926 --> 09:22.622
which this is obviously a useless door...

09:22.692 --> 09:24.422
you put a picture of someone...

09:24.492 --> 09:26.188
you have unresolved issues with...

09:26.259 --> 09:28.626
and it causes all of this weird energy flow.

09:28.692 --> 09:30.490
I don't even like being over here.

09:30.559 --> 09:33.188
- It's freaky.
- You shouldn't be over there then.

09:33.259 --> 09:34.852
- Every time you're-
- I'm sort of an empath.

09:34.926 --> 09:37.725
- Sort of an empath.
- And I can feel it. It's like a vortex.

09:38.992 --> 09:41.086
When was the last time
we were all together like this?

09:41.159 --> 09:43.253
I was thinking,
right before Thanksgiving...

09:43.326 --> 09:46.490
most of us were there,
but not everybody could be.

09:46.559 --> 09:48.050
I don't think Laurie- Laura?

09:48.126 --> 09:49.617
- Laurie.
- Laurie.

09:49.692 --> 09:51.661
Sorry.
We're gonna tell all these stories.

09:51.725 --> 09:53.387
We do that when we get together.

09:53.459 --> 09:55.587
So Laurie, what are you doing these days?

09:55.659 --> 09:57.651
- Well, I'm, uh-
- Keeping yourself busy?

09:57.725 --> 09:59.216
I'm keeping busy.

09:59.293 --> 10:01.421
I'm actually working
with some outreach programs in Silicon Valley.

10:01.492 --> 10:03.518
We work with at-risk youth.

10:03.592 --> 10:06.152
Oh, wow. Didn't you- No, no, no.

10:06.226 --> 10:08.195
Are you still teaching the yoga?

10:08.259 --> 10:10.387
The Spanish Yoga? The Spoga?

10:10.459 --> 10:12.860
- No. Not me.
- Are you sure that-

10:12.926 --> 10:14.622
Oh, that must've been another girl...

10:14.692 --> 10:17.856
that Kevin dated
that Amir is hooking up with.

10:17.926 --> 10:20.259
Wow. Let's give him a shovel.

10:20.326 --> 10:22.522
What are you doing?
What do you do for a living?

10:22.592 --> 10:25.357
I act. Shut up, guys.

10:25.426 --> 10:27.224
I didn't remember you were an actor.

10:27.293 --> 10:30.229
- So, you do mainly theater?
- Well, I did.

10:30.293 --> 10:34.822
Since I moved down here
to support my wife and her Skyping career.

10:34.892 --> 10:39.159
Um, but, no, I was in a TV show
for about four years.

10:39.226 --> 10:41.092
- Yeah? What was that?
- It was called Roswell.

10:41.159 --> 10:43.094
Oh, my God. I love Roswell.

10:43.159 --> 10:45.993
When were you on Roswell?
What episodes were you on?

10:46.059 --> 10:48.824
I was on all shows. Produced.

10:48.892 --> 10:51.225
- What do you mean?
- I was a series regular on that show.

10:51.293 --> 10:52.784
Yeah, he was, like, the main guy.

10:52.859 --> 10:54.350
What character did you play?

10:54.426 --> 10:57.919
- Joe.
- Did you have different hair, or something?

10:57.992 --> 10:59.483
I had the same exact hair.

10:59.559 --> 11:02.552
I'm sorry. Maybe it's
one of those things where you know...

11:02.625 --> 11:05.493
the character for so long, then you see someone
in person. It just doesn't compute.

11:05.559 --> 11:07.050
I don't know.

11:07.126 --> 11:11.655
- He's sort of grown into his face.
- You really have.

11:12.625 --> 11:14.218
Check it out again.

11:14.293 --> 11:17.229
I'm sure, you know, like the downward dog
probably gets to your head.

11:17.293 --> 11:19.694
- I didn't do yoga. That wasn't-
- Well, hey, listen.

11:19.759 --> 11:21.887
Thanks for enjoying the show.

11:21.959 --> 11:24.519
I think you are a really good actor...

11:24.592 --> 11:26.185
and I think you should continue doing it.

11:26.259 --> 11:29.320
- Thank you very much.
- I think it would be well worth your time.

11:29.393 --> 11:31.055
What are you up to these days?

11:31.126 --> 11:32.924
Last I remember, you were, like...

11:32.992 --> 11:35.325
taking the dance world by storm.

11:35.393 --> 11:37.294
Um, I guess the last time I saw you...

11:37.359 --> 11:40.022
must've been when
I was creating the dance show.

11:40.092 --> 11:41.151
Uh-huh.

11:41.226 --> 11:44.424
It was going really, really well for a while...

11:44.492 --> 11:47.929
but then, right before the, um-the premiere...

11:47.992 --> 11:50.587
they brought in Svetlana Aserrano...

11:50.659 --> 11:54.687
who is the best dancer in the world really...

11:54.759 --> 11:56.728
and they just offered me the understudy.

11:56.792 --> 11:58.556
[ Amir]
She should've been the whole thing.

11:58.625 --> 12:00.150
She created it. She should be...

12:00.226 --> 12:02.092
the prima ballerina of the San Francisco Ballet.

12:02.159 --> 12:04.890
- That's terrible.
- You know, you hear these stories sometimes...

12:04.959 --> 12:07.986
about people being
shut out of things they created...

12:08.059 --> 12:10.654
and I think it's horrible.
I'm sorry.

12:10.725 --> 12:14.924
But I mean it's a good lesson
that I had to learn, because-

12:14.992 --> 12:17.223
You know, because of my pride, I didn't want...

12:17.293 --> 12:19.387
to take the understudy and I took too long...

12:19.459 --> 12:23.328
to think about it and then
I lost the understudy job.

12:23.393 --> 12:28.024
- And they gave that to Katherine Meriss and-
- And she sucks.

12:28.092 --> 12:29.822
- She sucks.
- No, she's good, guys.

12:29.892 --> 12:31.690
Anyways, the reason that she's really big now...

12:31.759 --> 12:33.557
is because she ended up going up.

12:33.625 --> 12:35.150
Svetlana pulled out last minute...

12:35.226 --> 12:38.685
and Katherine ended up doing the show.

12:39.826 --> 12:41.988
- Katherine Meriss?
- Exactly.

12:42.059 --> 12:44.028
As soon as you said that, I thought,
"Katherine Meriss...

12:44.092 --> 12:46.618
that's pretty much the only person
in dance I'd know."

12:46.692 --> 12:48.627
Right. Well-

12:48.692 --> 12:52.527
So, she basically stole your-
your whole thing?

12:52.592 --> 12:55.391
Katherine Meriss has your life, basically.

12:56.259 --> 12:58.990
- Career.
- You have your life.

12:59.059 --> 13:01.756
It's a shame that it happened.
She doesn't hold a candle to you.

13:01.826 --> 13:05.024
Then, here's to the life that we do lead.

13:05.092 --> 13:06.583
- Yeah.
- Well said.

13:06.659 --> 13:09.322
- Here's to the comet.
- The comet. And the comet.

13:09.393 --> 13:11.362
Anybody have a happier story?

13:11.426 --> 13:13.554
Kevin, tell a crazy story,
first one that comes in your head.

13:13.625 --> 13:16.185
No. All right.

13:16.259 --> 13:19.024
Um-Sorry.

13:19.092 --> 13:20.617
I was going out with Laurie.

13:20.692 --> 13:23.218
We were drinking way too much at a bar.

13:23.293 --> 13:25.694
I passed out and I started dreaming...

13:25.759 --> 13:28.456
this big black bear...

13:28.525 --> 13:31.825
was up on its hind legs sort of mauling me.

13:31.892 --> 13:34.691
Slowly. Tenderly.

13:34.759 --> 13:36.318
Anyhow, we go to some party...

13:36.393 --> 13:38.191
in Santa Cruz and as we walked in...

13:38.259 --> 13:40.660
this huge dog comes running straight at me.

13:40.725 --> 13:43.092
Jumps up on its hind legs
and starts pawing me...

13:43.159 --> 13:46.618
exactly like the dream, and this guy yells...

13:46.692 --> 13:51.096
- "Bear, get down, Bear."
- What?

13:51.159 --> 13:53.719
Wow. You have a gift.

13:53.792 --> 13:55.693
The way you told that story, I thought...

13:55.759 --> 13:57.853
somebody was going to die.

13:57.926 --> 14:00.862
You know Bear is the most common dog name.

14:00.926 --> 14:03.259
Oh, that makes it a much less interesting story.

14:04.692 --> 14:06.388
Thanks for that, Lee.

14:06.459 --> 14:09.224
Most common bear name? Henry.

14:10.659 --> 14:13.561
- Look.
- Oh, my God.

14:13.625 --> 14:15.685
- What?
- This is like your phone.

14:15.759 --> 14:17.853
Oh, my God.
That happened to my phone tonight.

14:17.926 --> 14:20.361
And I was just holding mine in my hand.

14:20.426 --> 14:22.759
- Exact same thing.
- Shattered?

14:22.826 --> 14:24.988
Yeah. This is what they were
talking about on the news.

14:25.059 --> 14:26.960
Yeah. Yeah. It must be the comet.

14:27.026 --> 14:29.257
- The chicken tastes like tuna.
- All right.

14:29.326 --> 14:30.988
It must be Miller's Comet.

14:32.026 --> 14:33.824
So, nobody's phone works?

14:33.892 --> 14:35.758
I haven't checked mine, but I assume it doesn't.

14:35.826 --> 14:37.556
Everyone else's is in the other room.

14:37.625 --> 14:40.356
- Do you guys have a landline?
- No. We're wireless, baby.

14:42.092 --> 14:46.496
All right. I need to get ahold of my brother.

14:46.559 --> 14:49.051
- What about, um, your deal-
- The computer.

14:49.126 --> 14:50.651
- Good idea.
- It's in the office.

14:50.725 --> 14:52.216
- Could I?
- Yeah, yeah. Thanks.

14:52.293 --> 14:54.728
- What's wrong with your brother?
- Nothing. He's fine.

14:54.792 --> 14:58.024
He just, um-You know Brian.

14:58.092 --> 15:00.584
He hangs out with all those, you know,
theoretical physicists.

15:03.126 --> 15:05.186
- On the computer.
- How is there no Internet?

15:05.259 --> 15:08.024
- You run Skype. You tell us.
- I know.

15:08.092 --> 15:10.857
What are they saying about the comet?

15:10.926 --> 15:14.090
Nothing- Nothing to get upset about.

15:14.159 --> 15:16.560
He just said to give him a call...

15:16.625 --> 15:18.594
you know, if there was anything weird going on.

15:18.659 --> 15:20.389
Like, why?
What did he think it could do?

15:20.459 --> 15:21.950
[ Beth ]
Why didn't you tell me this?

15:22.026 --> 15:23.517
Because of your feng shui...

15:23.592 --> 15:26.027
- and granola candles, and I didn't want to-
- Stop making fun of me.

15:26.092 --> 15:27.583
I'm not making fun of you.

15:27.659 --> 15:29.150
There's a massive celestial object...

15:29.226 --> 15:30.717
and I didn't want to freak you out.

15:30.792 --> 15:32.283
- Now you're freaking me out.
- You guys realize...

15:32.359 --> 15:33.850
I was on a show called Roswell...

15:33.926 --> 15:36.327
and we tackled these issues every week.

15:36.393 --> 15:38.828
- That's true.
- [ Electrical Buzzing ]

15:38.892 --> 15:40.656
- Oh, shit.
- Oh, my God.

15:40.725 --> 15:42.660
- Honey.
- Um, I'm on it.

15:44.426 --> 15:45.917
I'm so glad I'm not high.

15:45.992 --> 15:49.429
I don't want to sit by the door to nowhere.

15:49.492 --> 15:53.088
Mike, check the breakers.

15:53.159 --> 15:55.424
I'm going to turn
the lighter on then come to you.

15:55.492 --> 15:58.257
- You guys need help?
- No. I have matches.

15:58.326 --> 16:00.989
- Candle power?
- I've got some over here.

16:01.059 --> 16:04.496
I got blue glow sticks,
red glow sticks and green glow sticks.

16:04.559 --> 16:07.290
Guys, let's just light candles and-

16:07.359 --> 16:09.225
[ All]
Oh. Ah.

16:09.293 --> 16:11.285
- Hey.
- Everybody rave.

16:11.359 --> 16:13.157
- Are you going outside?
- Yeah.

16:13.226 --> 16:14.717
What do you mean, you're going outside?

16:14.792 --> 16:16.852
I'm gonna see if the power's off
in the whole neighborhood.

16:16.926 --> 16:23.332
[ All Talking, Laughing ]

16:23.393 --> 16:26.090
I decided this is where mine goes.

16:26.159 --> 16:27.889
Well, this is a little strange...

16:27.959 --> 16:29.928
but the whole neighborhood is out...

16:29.992 --> 16:32.757
of power, except for a house
about two blocks up...

16:32.826 --> 16:34.351
which is completely lit up.

16:34.426 --> 16:36.054
It's kind of beautiful, actually.

16:36.126 --> 16:38.823
- The house?
- I want to go see.

16:38.892 --> 16:42.556
- Let's go check it out.
- I've never seen it so dark outside before.

16:42.625 --> 16:44.753
- You can't leave me. I'm gonna go.
- Come on then.

16:44.826 --> 16:46.317
Don't leave me by myself.

16:46.393 --> 16:49.329
- Where?
- You don't see it?

16:49.393 --> 16:51.919
- It's right there.
- Why are you so far ahead of everyone?

16:51.992 --> 16:53.961
Amir, dude, I can't see you.

16:54.026 --> 16:56.018
- Let Laurie go first.
- Thanks a lot.

16:56.092 --> 16:59.062
- That's sweet.
- Baby. Don't go.

16:59.126 --> 17:00.992
- Come here.
- See? Look.

17:01.059 --> 17:04.029
- Everything done.
- Come here.

17:06.226 --> 17:07.717
See that?

17:08.725 --> 17:11.058
- Two blocks down.
- Oh, they have light.

17:11.126 --> 17:13.823
- That one house has light.
- They must have a, uh-

17:13.892 --> 17:15.417
- A generator, or something?
- Yeah, yeah.

17:15.492 --> 17:16.983
What is that, two blocks away?

17:17.059 --> 17:18.550
Could solar power do that?

17:18.625 --> 17:20.890
But would their landline be working?

17:20.959 --> 17:22.450
Oh, wow. Look at that.

17:22.525 --> 17:25.757
- Oh, wow.
- It's magnificent.

17:25.826 --> 17:28.022
Holy moly.

17:31.326 --> 17:32.817
Well, I'm freezing.

17:32.892 --> 17:34.451
Should we head over there,
or should we-

17:34.525 --> 17:37.017
- No.
- Maybe we should head back inside.

17:37.092 --> 17:40.221
[ All Talking, Laughing ]

17:40.293 --> 17:41.727
- [ Door Closes]
- That was awesome, right?

17:41.792 --> 17:43.693
[ Laughing ]

17:43.759 --> 17:46.058
- I didn't even see this get knocked over.
- No.

17:46.126 --> 17:47.822
I didn't even know that glass was out here.

17:47.892 --> 17:49.451
I never go down into the basement.

17:49.525 --> 17:52.552
Guys, listen.
Seriously, what's up with that house?

17:52.625 --> 17:54.184
- Why are they-
- What?

17:54.259 --> 17:55.750
It could be a generator.

17:55.826 --> 17:57.089
Really?

17:57.159 --> 17:59.219
I don't know.
Maybe they're just off-the-grid bastard-

17:59.293 --> 18:00.818
Well, apparently, we have a generator.

18:00.892 --> 18:02.758
That would make sense
if they were off the grid.

18:02.826 --> 18:06.820
I'm actually thinking of- of going over there.

18:06.892 --> 18:08.383
What?

18:08.459 --> 18:11.054
- No, you're not going over there.
- Honey, it's okay.

18:11.126 --> 18:13.595
- It's o-
- It's ridiculous.

18:13.659 --> 18:16.094
It's not that far. Look, look, look, look.

18:18.525 --> 18:22.189
he said that if-
if anything strange were to happen...

18:22.259 --> 18:24.660
while the comet was passing over...

18:24.725 --> 18:27.889
- that we should stay inside.
- What?

18:27.959 --> 18:29.518
Just hold on, Amir.

18:29.592 --> 18:33.222
That we should stay inside
and that I should do my best to contact him.

18:33.293 --> 18:34.784
And so that's all that I'm doing.

18:34.859 --> 18:38.990
He said if anything strange should happen?
I mean-

18:39.059 --> 18:41.722
I'm not the only one
who thinks this is strange.

18:41.792 --> 18:43.727
- What is weird?
- [ Mike] Didn't he say to stay inside though?

18:43.792 --> 18:45.727
What's more important than the other?

18:45.792 --> 18:48.694
Yes, but this overrides that,
and it's only two blocks away.

18:48.759 --> 18:50.819
I'll be back in, like, five minutes.

18:50.892 --> 18:53.691
- Well, then you can't go by yourself.
- I'm going with him.

18:53.759 --> 18:56.160
There you go. I'll take Amir.

18:56.226 --> 18:58.627
- I'm the least important person here.
- This is true.

18:58.692 --> 19:00.285
It's about time
you started realizing that.

19:00.359 --> 19:03.193
- Just stay here.
- [ Laurie] Why are you going now?

19:03.259 --> 19:05.626
Well, bring your glow sticks
so we can identify your bodies.

19:05.692 --> 19:07.183
- Good idea.
- Thanks. That helps a lot.

19:08.492 --> 19:09.983
- Don't listen to them.
- That's great.

19:10.059 --> 19:11.550
Five minutes, all right?

19:11.625 --> 19:13.253
- Okay. Five minutes.
- All right. Okay.

19:13.326 --> 19:15.022
Beth, I-I couldn't find my shoes.

19:15.092 --> 19:16.583
I'm borrowing yours. I'm sorry.

19:16.659 --> 19:18.651
- [ Laughing ]
- That's so Amir.

19:20.126 --> 19:23.392
- Ten minutes we give them.
- They will be fine.

19:23.459 --> 19:26.429
We're just rattled because we're addicted
to cell phones and Internet.

19:26.492 --> 19:28.723
We are.
What did we do before cell phones?

19:28.792 --> 19:32.160
Em, you seem to be
the comet expert here tonight.

19:32.226 --> 19:33.717
What happened the last time?

19:33.792 --> 19:36.762
This one passed over a hundred years ago,
but much farther.

19:36.826 --> 19:38.988
But do we know
that anything happened?

19:39.059 --> 19:41.585
Nothing happened then. It was too far away.

19:41.659 --> 19:43.150
So, is there any reason...

19:43.226 --> 19:44.751
we should be freaked out right now?

19:44.826 --> 19:48.194
Well, I mean, it is a lot closer this time.

19:48.259 --> 19:50.023
What does that mean?

19:50.092 --> 19:51.788
Okay. I read one more thing.

19:51.859 --> 19:54.761
- Oh, another story.
- Just one more.

19:54.826 --> 19:56.488
It's called the Tunguska Event...

19:56.559 --> 19:59.495
and, um, it was a comet...

19:59.559 --> 20:01.323
or a meteor or something like that...

20:01.393 --> 20:03.988
that entered the atmosphere
over Siberia...

20:04.059 --> 20:06.961
and exploded over Earth.

20:07.026 --> 20:09.427
So, it didn't actually have physical impact.

20:09.492 --> 20:11.256
It didn't touch Earth.

20:11.326 --> 20:12.817
It didn't leave a crater or anything...

20:12.892 --> 20:15.361
but the force of that explosion...

20:15.426 --> 20:19.090
flattened trees for hundreds of miles.

20:19.159 --> 20:22.323
But it only killed about one to two people.

20:22.393 --> 20:25.363
It's Siberia.
There were probably only two people there.

20:25.426 --> 20:27.019
Yeah, but they don't necessarily-

20:27.092 --> 20:29.391
- It wiped out the population of Siberia.
- Basically. Yeah.

20:29.459 --> 20:31.189
- Right.
- Well, that doesn't make me feel better.

20:31.259 --> 20:32.921
And when was this?

20:32.992 --> 20:35.018
It was, like, in 1908, 1903-

20:35.092 --> 20:36.583
- [ Loud Boom at Front Door]
- [Screaming ]

20:36.659 --> 20:39.595
Oh, my God, oh, my God, oh, my God.
What is-

20:39.659 --> 20:42.959
- What the fuck was that?
- I don't know.

20:43.026 --> 20:44.995
- Lock that front door.
- Don't open the door.

20:45.059 --> 20:47.187
- I'm gonna get the bat.
- Yeah. Give me the bat.

20:47.259 --> 20:48.887
Mike, is that door locked?

20:48.959 --> 20:50.860
- I'll check it.
- Babe, stay away from the door.

20:50.926 --> 20:52.451
- You need the stick?
- Thank you.

20:52.525 --> 20:54.016
No, no, no.

20:54.092 --> 20:55.583
[ All Talking, Shouting ]

20:55.659 --> 20:58.219
- I just want to see what the hell is out there.
- Oh, my God.

20:59.393 --> 21:00.884
- [Whispers] Don't open it.
- Oh, God.

21:01.792 --> 21:03.624
Please, don't open that.

21:05.659 --> 21:08.458
- Is anybody there?
- Front door's locked. There's nothing.

21:08.525 --> 21:10.016
There's nothing out there.

21:10.092 --> 21:11.890
Thought I was going to have a heart attack.

21:11.959 --> 21:13.791
Everybody all right?

21:13.859 --> 21:16.761
Check the generator, please.
Please try the generator.

21:16.826 --> 21:18.556
- I'll check the generator.
- Would the guys do that?

21:18.625 --> 21:20.594
No. The guys would not do anything like that.

21:20.659 --> 21:22.150
They're not stupid. They wouldn't do that.

21:22.226 --> 21:23.922
- How long have they been gone?
- Like ten minutes.

21:23.992 --> 21:26.723
Five minutes out, five minutes back.
They should be back by now.

21:26.792 --> 21:28.283
So, they should be back by now.

21:28.359 --> 21:30.760
- Okay. I think we should go get them.
- No, no, no.

21:30.826 --> 21:32.317
I want to go get my husband.

21:32.393 --> 21:34.225
We need to do it together this time, guys.

21:34.293 --> 21:36.057
That's fine with me. I just want to go.

21:36.126 --> 21:39.187
- Don't go outside.
- I'm not going anywhere. I'm just-

21:39.259 --> 21:43.196
We should go get them.
We can all go together.

21:44.059 --> 21:47.052
Okay, all right. This is good.

21:47.126 --> 21:49.561
Is that the grid or the generator?

21:49.625 --> 21:51.491
No, it's just us. He must have gotten it going.

21:51.559 --> 21:53.050
There's no other lights on?
It's just us?

21:53.126 --> 21:56.187
- It's pitch black out there. At least it's on.
- So it must be-

21:57.359 --> 21:58.850
- Well done.
- Thank you.

21:58.926 --> 22:01.418
- You did it.
- Let there be light.

22:01.492 --> 22:04.758
Okay. Well, I think that we should-

22:04.826 --> 22:07.625
As a group, we should go find those guys.

22:07.692 --> 22:10.628
- I agree.
- Let's do it as a group this time.

22:10.692 --> 22:12.422
No. That's ridiculous.

22:12.492 --> 22:14.461
If you get lost in the woods,
you're supposed...

22:14.525 --> 22:16.391
to stay where you are
until someone can find you.

22:16.459 --> 22:18.928
Fine. That's great.
Let's just sit down and breathe.

22:18.992 --> 22:22.190
For once, I actually agree
with what you're saying.

22:22.259 --> 22:24.592
You know what?
You've been giving me shit all night.

22:24.659 --> 22:27.754
- I am agreeing with you.
- Guys, guys, guys.

22:29.492 --> 22:31.154
I don't like any of this.

22:31.226 --> 22:33.957
- [ Doorbell Rings]
- Jesus!

22:35.026 --> 22:36.517
Stay.

22:36.592 --> 22:38.493
Oh, my God.

22:39.792 --> 22:41.351
Oh man, it's them.

22:43.159 --> 22:45.060
- What the hell happened?
- Are you okay?

22:45.126 --> 22:48.688
- I'm fine, I'm fine.
- Are you okay?

22:48.759 --> 22:50.250
What is this?

22:50.326 --> 22:52.022
[ All Talking ]

22:52.092 --> 22:54.891
- What's the box?
- That was at the other house.

22:54.959 --> 22:56.484
I thought I saw Hugh put it down.

22:56.559 --> 22:58.323
Then he was running around the corner and-

22:58.393 --> 23:00.385
- You just took it?
- I just followed him.

23:00.459 --> 23:02.690
- I didn't- I had it in my hand.
- Why was he running?

23:02.759 --> 23:05.251
- Hugh, what happened?
- I'm fine, I'm fine.

23:05.326 --> 23:08.660
- Did you put this down?
- Amir, why the fuck did you take that?

23:08.725 --> 23:11.490
- I thought I saw you put it down.
- I did not touch that thing.

23:11.559 --> 23:13.994
I don't know what that is or why you grabbed it.

23:14.059 --> 23:17.188
- Guys, what happened?
- Okay. We were at the other house.

23:17.259 --> 23:19.888
Hugh went around the side.
I thought I heard a noise.

23:19.959 --> 23:22.519
You made some kind of sound,
and then you saw what? Something.

23:22.592 --> 23:24.083
You won't tell me what you saw.

23:24.159 --> 23:27.152
I don't understand what's going on.
What did you see?

23:27.226 --> 23:28.717
- I don't-
- What did you see?

23:28.792 --> 23:30.283
That has nothing to do with anything...

23:30.359 --> 23:31.918
that we should be fucking concerned with.

23:31.992 --> 23:33.756
What did you see?

23:33.826 --> 23:36.887
- It's not a big deal. I'll walk it back.
- Okay, fine.

23:36.959 --> 23:38.689
Wait. Let me open it first.

23:38.759 --> 23:40.489
No, Mike. What are you doing?

23:40.559 --> 23:43.393
- What is it?
- I don't know. I don't know.

23:43.459 --> 23:46.054
You don't want to talk
about it and you don't want to open-

23:46.126 --> 23:49.062
Fine! Open the fucking box!
Open the box. What do I care?

23:49.126 --> 23:51.027
[ Beth ]
What is wrong? Calm down.

23:51.092 --> 23:53.755
What happened?

23:53.826 --> 23:55.317
Holy shit, it worked.

23:56.459 --> 23:57.950
I got it.

23:58.026 --> 23:59.517
Open it away from your face.

23:59.592 --> 24:02.027
- It's not a bomb.
- How do you know what the heck it is?

24:02.092 --> 24:05.460
- Don't freak out.
- Be careful.

24:07.759 --> 24:11.025
- Oh, my God, It's a ping-pong paddle.
- It's a ping-pong paddle.

24:11.092 --> 24:14.153
- Well, what's that?
- What is going on?

24:18.126 --> 24:20.891
- Oh, my God.
- What is it?

24:20.959 --> 24:24.657
These are pictures of all of us.

24:25.892 --> 24:29.192
These are...

24:29.259 --> 24:31.592
- Somebody's marked us.
- I want to try to figure this out.

24:31.659 --> 24:33.594
- This is insane.
- And there are numbers on the back.

24:33.659 --> 24:35.423
- Hugh.
- Baby, what did you see?

24:35.492 --> 24:37.324
- Hugh what did you see?
- What did you see?

24:37.393 --> 24:38.884
Jesus Christ, man.

24:38.959 --> 24:42.054
You can't stand there and not say anything!
What did you see?

24:44.426 --> 24:45.917
Hugh!

24:47.159 --> 24:49.651
There are pictures of us in this box!

24:49.725 --> 24:51.216
Hugh!

25:00.559 --> 25:03.688
I went to the window,
and I looked in the window.

25:03.759 --> 25:06.160
And I saw a table...

25:06.226 --> 25:10.061
with wine glasses and candles...

25:10.126 --> 25:15.190
and dinner set for eight people.

25:15.259 --> 25:17.228
I saw-

25:19.559 --> 25:21.050
Oh, my God.

25:21.126 --> 25:23.220
Right. Okay, fuck you, Hugh.

25:23.293 --> 25:24.886
- I saw-
- Bullshit.

25:24.959 --> 25:27.952
- Did you guys come and fuck with this door?
- Fuck you, Kevin.

25:28.026 --> 25:31.394
- Did you come to the side door?
- No. You went to the side door
at the other house.

25:31.459 --> 25:33.155
They wouldn't answer the door, so I went-

25:33.226 --> 25:35.752
- Bullshit.
- [ All Talking ]

25:35.826 --> 25:38.261
You dipshits walked in a circle
and knocked on this door.

25:38.326 --> 25:40.557
I did not walk in a fucking circle!
I went two blocks.

25:40.625 --> 25:42.685
We went up to that house.
I knocked at the door.

25:42.759 --> 25:45.354
Nobody answered,
so I went and banged on the side door.

25:45.426 --> 25:47.952
- Did you see yourself, Hugh?
- No, I did not see myself.

25:48.026 --> 25:51.155
- No, because you weren't there.
- I did not go in a circle!

25:51.892 --> 25:53.383
- Fuck.
- Just calm down.

25:54.326 --> 25:55.817
I don't believe this.

25:55.892 --> 25:57.383
This still doesn't explain the pictures.

25:57.459 --> 25:59.052
What's on the back of them?

25:59.126 --> 26:00.924
Numbers.

26:00.992 --> 26:06.397
They're all-We've got two, one, one.

26:06.459 --> 26:08.985
That's five.

26:09.059 --> 26:11.927
- Whoa, whoa, whoa. Where are you going?
- I'm gonna go back over there.

26:11.992 --> 26:14.985
- Whoa.
- No, no, no. Think about it.

26:15.059 --> 26:17.324
I'm gonna go back over there.
I'm gonna ask to use their phone...

26:17.393 --> 26:19.225
and, hopefully, I can get
in touch with my brother.

26:19.293 --> 26:21.922
- And if they're not there,
I'll just leave a note. Right?
- No.

26:21.992 --> 26:23.483
No, no, no. That makes sense. Right?

26:23.559 --> 26:25.994
- You should not go back.
- It's fine. It'll be fine.

26:30.859 --> 26:32.521
What's a note going to do?

26:36.393 --> 26:40.922
If these people have pictures of us,
they might be crazy.

26:40.992 --> 26:42.483
Shit! There's someone out there.

26:42.559 --> 26:44.050
There's someone out there.

26:44.126 --> 26:46.595
- What?
- Oh, my God.

26:46.659 --> 26:48.389
Oh, there's a big guy
at the door.

26:48.459 --> 26:50.485
- Oh, my God.
- At the door?

26:50.559 --> 26:52.050
What should we do?

26:52.126 --> 26:53.617
- He's walking away. He's walking away.
- Please, please.

26:53.692 --> 26:55.217
- Baby, please be careful.
- Oh, my God.

27:01.725 --> 27:03.284
- Baby.
- Careful.

27:03.359 --> 27:04.850
- Shit.
- What?

27:12.293 --> 27:14.694
What is it, babe?

27:16.659 --> 27:21.063
"Hey, there. Don't mean to freak you guys out...

27:21.126 --> 27:25.564
but we just wanted to borrow your phone
for five minutes tops.

27:25.625 --> 27:27.287
Thanks."

27:36.326 --> 27:37.988
Two kinds.

27:38.059 --> 27:40.358
Regular Band-Aid or cloth?

27:42.026 --> 27:44.222
Uh, whatever.

27:44.293 --> 27:46.922
- Cloth.
- Okay. Here we go.

27:48.092 --> 27:50.721
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

27:50.792 --> 27:56.026
These are ones.
This is a two. We are four, five, six.

27:56.092 --> 27:58.027
Do you have any red markers?

27:58.092 --> 28:01.893
Okay. Why are these three ones?

28:02.859 --> 28:05.522
- This is a six. Five.
- Hugh and Lee.

28:05.592 --> 28:07.083
Two.

28:08.492 --> 28:10.290
Four.

28:10.359 --> 28:12.328
And that's the same picture.

28:12.393 --> 28:15.261
Oh, my God.

28:16.859 --> 28:18.350
Somebody cut that in half.

28:22.492 --> 28:24.358
Where are these from?

28:24.426 --> 28:27.260
[ Beth ]
Could this be like numerology?

28:27.326 --> 28:29.921
Like if you add up all the numbers...

28:29.992 --> 28:31.722
in your name and the birthday-

28:31.792 --> 28:33.761
Like life path numbers or something like that?

28:33.826 --> 28:36.352
If that's the case, then they're just crazy
and it doesn't matter anyway.

28:36.426 --> 28:38.588
So, what do all the ones have in common?

28:38.659 --> 28:41.458
- Um, we have Lee-
- Date of birth?

28:41.525 --> 28:43.426
- Oldest to youngest?
- There's no three?

28:43.492 --> 28:45.654
- There's no three.
- There's no three.

28:45.725 --> 28:49.492
Is there someone-
Is there someone that would want to be...

28:49.559 --> 28:51.050
doing this to us?

28:51.126 --> 28:54.494
Is there someone
that is on someone's bad side?

28:54.559 --> 28:57.427
- What?
- This was taken tonight.

28:57.492 --> 29:00.428
- What?
- How do you know that?

29:00.492 --> 29:04.657
I bought this sweater today,
so that's from tonight.

29:06.393 --> 29:08.589
Has anyone taken a picture of you tonight?

29:10.092 --> 29:12.527
Someone took a picture
of you when you were looking at the box.

29:12.592 --> 29:14.220
You were looking into the lens.

29:14.293 --> 29:16.592
But then it was already in the box.

29:16.659 --> 29:19.720
What is that?

29:19.792 --> 29:21.283
I can't tell what that is.

29:21.359 --> 29:23.419
There's dots on the wall
and there's a lampshade.

29:23.492 --> 29:25.222
None of the others are from tonight.
Right?

29:25.293 --> 29:28.229
[ Em ]
No. This our picture. This is from last fall.

29:28.293 --> 29:30.728
- This picture of Amir was taken over here.
- How do you know that?

29:30.792 --> 29:32.852
- He's standing in front of this drum.
- Guys, hang on.

29:32.926 --> 29:34.417
I can't figure out what this is.

29:34.492 --> 29:36.085
It's taken from the door?

29:36.159 --> 29:37.593
So, from behind the curtain?

29:37.659 --> 29:39.150
It's taken from over there.

29:39.226 --> 29:41.695
Wait. When someone knocked on the door,
were you there?

29:41.759 --> 29:43.523
You were gone.

29:43.592 --> 29:45.891
But you're looking right at the camera.

29:47.792 --> 29:51.627
So, it would be from that door,
then. Right?

29:51.692 --> 29:53.320
You don't remember- I mean...

29:53.393 --> 29:56.056
this is you, man. This is you.

29:56.126 --> 29:58.721
Guys, this isn't going to solve anything.

29:59.725 --> 30:01.216
What're you doing?

30:01.293 --> 30:03.819
- I need a drink.
- I need something.

30:03.892 --> 30:05.656
The-The pictures?

30:05.725 --> 30:07.557
All right. Me too.

30:14.792 --> 30:16.988
It looks like my handwriting, babe.

30:17.059 --> 30:18.857
Look at this.

30:23.992 --> 30:26.052
It looks like I wrote this.

30:26.126 --> 30:27.958
Okay, relax.

30:28.026 --> 30:30.928
You're starting to freak me out.

30:30.992 --> 30:32.483
That's your handwriting.

30:37.326 --> 30:39.227
What is going on?

30:42.692 --> 30:45.218
I feel like I'm losing my mind.

30:51.826 --> 30:54.057
I can't stop thinking about the fact that you...

30:54.126 --> 30:58.826
brought up a story you shared with Laurie.

31:00.226 --> 31:03.253
Of all the stories that you could've-

31:03.326 --> 31:05.454
All the experiences that we've shared...

31:05.525 --> 31:07.084
you brought up a story about her?

31:07.159 --> 31:09.390
- I am so sorry.
- In front of everyone.

31:09.459 --> 31:12.258
It's a crazy story.
We don't have stories like that.

31:12.326 --> 31:14.227
Oh, they're not crazy enough for you.

31:14.293 --> 31:16.762
- Baby, it's a good thing.
- Oh, God.

31:16.826 --> 31:18.818
I don't need crazy stories like that anymore.

31:18.892 --> 31:22.556
All right. Hey, um, fuck this.
Let's just- Let's go.

31:22.625 --> 31:24.287
I'm gonna go over there and, theoretically...

31:24.359 --> 31:26.692
let's go see if our
theoretical selves are there.

31:26.759 --> 31:28.352
- No, no, no.
- I'm going.

31:28.426 --> 31:31.794
- I'm in.
- There's some weird stuff happening here.

31:31.859 --> 31:33.350
I think we should-

31:33.426 --> 31:34.917
- I think we should evaluate-
- Please, can we-

31:34.992 --> 31:36.858
- I just evaluated and I'm going.
- Can we stay here?

31:36.926 --> 31:39.418
- If there's another me, I want to see me.
- No. No way.

31:39.492 --> 31:41.085
- No, no.
- Let's go.

31:41.159 --> 31:42.650
- Look.
- I'm over this.

31:42.725 --> 31:44.421
I'm getting sick of talking about it.

31:44.492 --> 31:46.017
I'm getting sick of writing about it.

31:46.092 --> 31:48.721
- The same fucking paper, the pictures-
- Wait.

31:48.792 --> 31:50.693
There's nobody trying to hurt us.

31:50.759 --> 31:52.819
We go find out
what the hell is going on.

31:52.892 --> 31:55.794
What about you?
You were the one who wanted to go.

31:55.859 --> 31:58.590
That's when I thought they might have a phone.

31:58.659 --> 32:02.824
- Four glow sticks.
- Can we please keep two guys here?

32:02.892 --> 32:05.225
- Two guys staying here? Please?
- I'm staying, I'm staying.

32:05.293 --> 32:07.524
- Are you going?
- Amir, please.

32:07.592 --> 32:09.322
Let's go.

32:09.393 --> 32:10.884
So, what? We're splitting up again?

32:10.959 --> 32:12.450
No. We're not splitting up.

32:12.525 --> 32:15.359
- We're just gonna go in two different groups.
- Oh. Okay.

32:15.426 --> 32:17.224
Sticks, sticks, sticks.

32:17.293 --> 32:18.784
Do we need a towel on it?

32:18.859 --> 32:21.090
[ Em ]
I'm coming. Wait.

32:21.159 --> 32:23.355
Chill for a second. I'm coming.

32:23.426 --> 32:25.224
- Why?
- Because I want to go.

32:25.293 --> 32:26.886
I'm going with Kevin.

32:30.659 --> 32:33.219
- Give us 20 minutes.
- All right.

32:33.293 --> 32:35.728
- And then what?
- Are we taking the bat?

32:35.792 --> 32:38.421
- No. We'll be fine.
- You will be fine. It's gonna be all right.

32:38.492 --> 32:40.085
We'll find out what's going on.

32:49.159 --> 32:52.721
No cars. No people. There's nothing.

33:12.393 --> 33:13.884
[Quietly]
Guys, look.

33:15.226 --> 33:17.286
That's my house.

33:18.625 --> 33:21.220
- Mike.
- This is my house.

33:24.725 --> 33:26.557
Mike, this isn't right.

33:26.625 --> 33:29.094
[Whispering ]
Mike, this is not your house.

33:29.159 --> 33:30.650
Mike.

33:32.992 --> 33:34.984
- My house.
- This is not your house, Mike.

33:35.059 --> 33:38.154
- Mike.
- This is not your house.

33:38.226 --> 33:41.492
[Whispering continues]
What is he doing? Kevin.

33:43.092 --> 33:46.085
- I see- I see Lee.
- Guys.

33:47.892 --> 33:51.124
- We have to go.
- Let's get out of here now.

33:51.193 --> 33:53.128
Mike, we need to get the hell out of here.

33:53.193 --> 33:54.991
[Whispering ]
Someone's coming.

33:55.059 --> 33:57.426
Someone's coming. Go. Just go.

34:15.492 --> 34:17.723
[ Heavy Breathing ]

34:34.559 --> 34:37.586
[ Panting ]

34:42.226 --> 34:43.717
That's just nuts.

34:46.359 --> 34:49.090
So, you saw four figures, same as you?

34:49.159 --> 34:52.254
Except they had red glow sticks.

34:52.326 --> 34:54.158
Who had red glow sticks?

34:54.226 --> 34:56.024
They had the red glow sticks.

34:56.092 --> 34:58.721
We had the blue glow sticks.
That was the only difference.

34:58.792 --> 35:01.261
So, they must've opened the red box
when the lights went out.

35:01.326 --> 35:04.057
- And you didn't say anything to them?
- Would you?

35:04.126 --> 35:05.617
No, I wouldn't.

35:05.692 --> 35:08.252
I think I would've thought I was going to die,
or something.

35:08.326 --> 35:10.124
Okay, okay. So, that's it?

35:10.193 --> 35:13.027
Well, that and there's this weird zone...

35:13.092 --> 35:14.788
that's even darker than the rest of it all.

35:14.859 --> 35:17.226
[ Hugh ]
We went through that.

35:17.293 --> 35:19.057
We went through that
when we went down there.

35:19.126 --> 35:21.425
We need to find out what's going on.

35:21.492 --> 35:23.586
- The Internet's down. We don't have-
- We can't just sit here.

35:23.659 --> 35:26.424
What else? Do you guys have any-

35:26.492 --> 35:28.154
Do you have books?

35:28.226 --> 35:29.717
Books on what? Books on comets?

35:29.792 --> 35:31.317
Comets, gravity, black holes-

35:31.393 --> 35:34.261
Yeah, I've got Shakespeare,
some Henry Miller and some screenplays.

35:34.326 --> 35:35.817
Dude, I'm a fucking actor.

35:35.892 --> 35:38.225
Anything about quantum physics?

35:38.293 --> 35:40.728
Yeah, that's right up my alley.

35:40.792 --> 35:43.193
Some actors read.

35:43.259 --> 35:46.525
Your brother left a book at our house and-

35:46.592 --> 35:48.185
What?

35:48.259 --> 35:49.750
I put it in an envelope to mail...

35:49.826 --> 35:51.522
but I-I put it in your car.

35:51.592 --> 35:53.584
- And it's about?
- I don't know what it's about.

35:53.659 --> 35:55.184
- Comets?
- It's just one of his books.

35:55.259 --> 35:57.057
It's always about stuff like that.

35:57.126 --> 35:59.891
Yeah, I will-
I will go get the book I don't know about.

35:59.959 --> 36:02.986
- Can somebody go with him?
- Could you bring the bat?

36:03.059 --> 36:05.392
- Yeah.
- Yes. That's a good idea.

36:05.459 --> 36:07.360
Please be careful, babe.

36:08.725 --> 36:10.489
Okay.

36:10.559 --> 36:12.152
Should we wake up Lee?

36:12.226 --> 36:15.196
How could she go to sleep
in the middle of all this?

36:15.259 --> 36:16.955
[Shrieks]

36:17.026 --> 36:18.927
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, babe.

36:20.792 --> 36:22.761
Jesus. Calm down, everybody.

36:22.826 --> 36:24.317
Oh, baby.

36:24.393 --> 36:26.521
I was gonna mail it back to him.

36:32.159 --> 36:33.650
What is it?

36:33.725 --> 36:37.423
"Gravitation: An Introduction
To Current Research."

36:37.492 --> 36:39.085
That's not gonna apply.

36:39.159 --> 36:41.924
[ Laurie] So, is his brother like
a scientist, or something?

36:41.992 --> 36:43.483
He's just a really trippy guy.

36:43.559 --> 36:45.050
He's really, really smart, a real egghead.

36:45.126 --> 36:48.494
But it's hard to-
It's like he thinks out loud.

36:48.559 --> 36:51.927
- He's a teacher at U.C.S.D.
- What do you got, Hugh?

36:51.992 --> 36:54.154
This is, uh-

36:54.226 --> 36:58.186
These are Brian's notes
from his lesson plan for his class.

36:58.259 --> 37:01.718
"Decoherence and Schrödinger's Cat."
He talked about this.

37:01.792 --> 37:05.251
- Do you guys know what Schrödinger's cat is?
- I'm allergic.

37:05.326 --> 37:08.785
So, it's a, um- It's a thought experiment.

37:08.859 --> 37:10.487
There's a-There's a cat in a box...

37:10.559 --> 37:13.529
that has, like, a 50/50 chance of living...

37:13.592 --> 37:15.083
because there's a vial of poison...

37:15.159 --> 37:16.684
that's also in the box.

37:16.759 --> 37:20.218
So, regular physics would say
that it's one or the other.

37:20.293 --> 37:21.784
That the cat is either alive or dead.

37:21.859 --> 37:24.624
But Brian would argue
that quantum physics says...

37:24.692 --> 37:27.526
that both realities exist simultaneously.

37:27.592 --> 37:31.051
It's only when you open the box
that they collapse...

37:31.126 --> 37:33.095
into a single event. Right?

37:33.159 --> 37:36.357
So, listen to this. This is what he's written.

37:36.426 --> 37:37.917
"There is another theory:

37:37.992 --> 37:39.984
that two states continue to exist...

37:40.059 --> 37:42.221
separate and decoherent from each other...

37:42.293 --> 37:44.819
each creating a new branch of reality...

37:44.892 --> 37:46.485
based on the two outcomes.

37:46.559 --> 37:49.586
Quantum decoherence ensures
that the different outcomes...

37:49.659 --> 37:52.356
have no interaction with each other."

37:52.426 --> 37:54.691
- Hold on.
- Well, that explains it.

37:54.759 --> 37:59.322
So we're in the box. We're the cat.

37:59.393 --> 38:02.192
We're both alive and dead.

38:02.259 --> 38:07.095
So, there are-
There are two separate realities, and-

38:07.159 --> 38:10.027
presumably until the comet passes.

38:10.092 --> 38:12.323
- Until the comet passes?
- Okay.

38:12.393 --> 38:16.023
Or decoherence is maintained
and those two separate realities...

38:16.092 --> 38:18.084
will remain separate once the comet passes.

38:18.159 --> 38:19.650
Everybody will be fine.

38:19.725 --> 38:21.523
Decoherence keeps us separate.

38:21.592 --> 38:23.151
Right.

38:23.226 --> 38:27.027
Why are the other us
contacting us then in this way?

38:27.092 --> 38:28.583
They didn't want to.

38:28.659 --> 38:30.890
Who got the pictures? Who-The numbers?

38:30.959 --> 38:34.452
We started it when we went to find
a house with lights.

38:34.525 --> 38:36.960
Yeah, maybe they didn't mean the box for us.

38:37.026 --> 38:39.518
The box isn't for us.

38:39.592 --> 38:43.427
What if we've already interacted
with ourselves?

38:43.492 --> 38:46.087
So, we're collapsing on ourselves right now.

38:46.159 --> 38:48.993
Not if we stay separate from each other.

38:49.059 --> 38:51.119
It's already too late. We've already been there.

38:51.193 --> 38:54.459
Do you remember that movie Sliding Doors?

38:54.525 --> 38:57.586
Where just a fraction of a second...

38:57.659 --> 38:59.525
there could be two realities?

38:59.592 --> 39:02.585
In one, she runs and tries
to get on the subway and she can't.

39:02.659 --> 39:04.184
She gets her hand stuck in the door.

39:04.259 --> 39:06.023
In the other one,
she gets through and there's two-

39:06.092 --> 39:08.391
If we're collapsing right now,
I'm gonna collapse on them.

39:08.459 --> 39:10.189
I'm not gonna wait for them
to collapse on us.

39:12.492 --> 39:14.461
I'll go over there and I'll just kill 'em.

39:14.525 --> 39:17.017
- What?
- Half-kidding.

39:17.092 --> 39:18.583
- Mike, let's just-
- I love my fucking life.

39:18.659 --> 39:21.060
Let's be smart first
before we do anything stupid...

39:21.126 --> 39:22.617
and let's stick with that we do know.

39:22.692 --> 39:25.491
And what's smart?
Just sitting here? Doing nothing?

39:25.559 --> 39:27.994
What we do know is that we took
this box. Right?

39:28.059 --> 39:30.392
So, our first act
should be to return it. Yes?

39:30.459 --> 39:32.360
Fuck that. No.
We're not returning that box.

39:32.426 --> 39:34.258
I don't trust that house. That stays here.

39:34.326 --> 39:36.557
- Wait, wait, wait.
- What's got you so freaked out?

39:36.625 --> 39:39.185
- Stupid, stupid question.
- You're right.

39:39.259 --> 39:41.592
We're not at war
with the house down the street.

39:41.659 --> 39:44.891
They might literally be the same people as us.

39:44.959 --> 39:46.723
Mike's saying come over here
and let's kill us.

39:46.792 --> 39:51.787
That's right. If you do it
first, you know who you're gonna fight?

39:51.859 --> 39:53.350
- Mike.
- You.

39:53.426 --> 39:55.588
You're gonna run into you.

39:56.826 --> 39:58.590
Who's gonna win that?

39:59.826 --> 40:01.988
Who did you see in the window
when you went there?

40:02.059 --> 40:03.891
- Did you see yourself?
- I did not see myself.

40:03.959 --> 40:05.450
- I told you who I saw.
- Okay, okay.

40:05.525 --> 40:10.156
But what if, in that over there, that house,
what if I'm drinking?

40:10.226 --> 40:12.354
I mean, just think about that for a sec.

40:15.092 --> 40:17.152
That's a fucked-up Michael.

40:17.226 --> 40:19.218
Oh, God.

40:19.293 --> 40:21.057
I'm not gonna wait for a fucking drunk Mike...

40:21.126 --> 40:22.617
to come over here and kill me.

40:22.692 --> 40:25.059
And kill you and kill you
and kill you.

40:28.459 --> 40:30.052
I'm not waiting for that.

40:31.193 --> 40:33.594
Wait, wait, wait a minute.

40:33.659 --> 40:35.525
Who did you see when you were there?

40:35.592 --> 40:40.963
I saw Amir, I saw Hugh, and I saw Lee.

40:41.026 --> 40:42.927
Okay. Lee's not here right now.

40:42.992 --> 40:45.257
- She's taking a nap.
- What do you mean, she's taking a nap?

40:45.326 --> 40:48.057
- So, it's different, then.
- Something's off. It's not the same.

40:48.126 --> 40:49.651
In this reality, Lee's napping.

40:49.725 --> 40:52.388
Maybe in that reality, you're napping?

40:52.459 --> 40:53.950
So, that's why Mike didn't see her.

40:54.026 --> 40:57.155
Right, and if Beth is napping in that reality...

40:58.559 --> 41:00.050
they don't have the book.

41:00.126 --> 41:01.617
- They don't.
- Right.

41:01.692 --> 41:03.251
The other house doesn't have the book.

41:03.326 --> 41:04.885
And if they don't have the book...

41:04.959 --> 41:08.623
they're not having this conversation right now.

41:08.692 --> 41:11.355
So, then if we get the book from the car...

41:11.426 --> 41:13.622
then we can avoid all this.

41:13.692 --> 41:15.183
Take it? Take their book?

41:15.259 --> 41:16.750
It's a possibility.

41:18.359 --> 41:20.851
- Hugh, give me your keys.
- No, no, no. Wait, wait, wait.

41:20.926 --> 41:25.227
- We're not supposed to mess with any of this.
- Why would we even risk this?

41:25.293 --> 41:27.694
- He's talking about going over
and fighting them.
- But why make it worse?

41:27.759 --> 41:29.955
Because then I don't
have to go over there and kill them.

41:30.026 --> 41:31.517
Just give me the keys.

41:31.592 --> 41:34.756
No. I don't think
that we should do anything.

41:34.826 --> 41:36.692
And you are not taking my keys.

41:43.892 --> 41:45.690
Where you going, Mike?

41:47.126 --> 41:48.617
How do we know it's exactly us?

41:48.692 --> 41:51.753
What if it's just externals?
What if-

41:51.826 --> 41:53.488
- The dark side of us.
- Yeah.

41:53.559 --> 41:56.996
- It's us, you guys.
- You mean, the not friendly versions?

41:57.059 --> 42:01.019
Well, if it's us,
then this could be- Is it a good thing?

42:01.092 --> 42:03.425
It sounds like it would be a way to reach...

42:03.492 --> 42:05.085
higher consciousness, if we want to-

42:05.159 --> 42:06.923
Like an acceptance of ourselves?

42:06.992 --> 42:09.962
Well, yeah. We always talk about
meeting ourselves and finding ourselves...

42:10.026 --> 42:11.517
and here we have an opportunity...

42:11.592 --> 42:14.084
to actually physically find ourselves.

42:14.159 --> 42:15.684
That's a lot of pressure.

42:15.759 --> 42:18.422
- Look who's joined us.
- Hi, everybody.

42:18.492 --> 42:20.552
- How are you, honey?
- Okay.

42:20.625 --> 42:22.184
Welcome back to your own dinner party.

42:22.259 --> 42:24.421
Yeah. How's my dinner party going?

42:24.492 --> 42:27.018
- Super missed you.
- It's going.

42:27.092 --> 42:28.583
[Whispers]
I have an idea.

42:28.659 --> 42:30.685
I have an idea that will prevent them...

42:30.759 --> 42:32.694
from getting the book from the car.

42:32.759 --> 42:34.421
What are you talking about, man?

42:34.492 --> 42:37.291
I'm gonna go to that house,
and I'm gonna blackmail myself.

42:37.359 --> 42:39.351
I'm gonna leave a note to keep Mike...

42:39.426 --> 42:41.418
from having them go to the car
to get that book.

42:41.492 --> 42:43.222
What do you mean, a blackmail note?

42:43.293 --> 42:44.955
Something I know
that I don't want revealed.

42:45.026 --> 42:46.517
What are you talking about?

42:46.592 --> 42:48.220
The thing with Beth.

42:48.293 --> 42:49.921
The thing with Beth?

42:49.992 --> 42:52.154
I thought you and Hugh
worked that out years ago.

42:52.226 --> 42:54.422
This is the worst idea I've ever heard.

42:54.492 --> 42:56.256
It's amazing, 'cause it would work on me.

42:56.326 --> 42:58.693
- Going over there-
- It's the same person.

42:58.759 --> 43:00.250
We don't-You don't know that.

43:00.326 --> 43:01.988
- This will pass.
- It's brilliant.

43:02.059 --> 43:03.925
- No. It is not brilliant.
- It's brilliant.

43:03.992 --> 43:06.518
Dude, no.
I know this look in your eye.

43:06.592 --> 43:08.686
Mike, no.

43:08.759 --> 43:10.694
Why would he even say that?

43:10.759 --> 43:12.250
Divergence.
Otherwise, it's just the same people.

43:12.326 --> 43:13.817
What's going on?

43:13.892 --> 43:15.383
[ Hugh ]
And if it's the same people...

43:15.459 --> 43:17.428
then why not just leave each other alone?

43:17.492 --> 43:19.085
That's what I would want me to do.

43:19.159 --> 43:20.650
That might be the best thing to do.

43:20.725 --> 43:22.489
Right? You doing okay?

43:22.559 --> 43:24.050
Yeah, yeah.

43:24.126 --> 43:28.188
I don't know if I'm
woozy from the drops or if it's like-

43:28.259 --> 43:29.989
- What drops?
- What drops?

43:30.059 --> 43:32.290
- Um-
- Did you give her-

43:32.359 --> 43:34.760
[ Beth ]
Yeah, well. She wanted to take-

43:34.826 --> 43:37.728
I just felt so weird before.

43:37.792 --> 43:41.888
- It's this stuff I brought, this rescue remedy.
- What is it?

43:41.959 --> 43:46.454
It's got echinacea, golden seal, passion flower
and a little ketamine.

43:46.525 --> 43:49.085
I swear to God.

43:49.159 --> 43:50.855
- Ketamine?
- A little ketamine?

43:50.926 --> 43:53.361
- It's not like you're going to go into this-
- Beth.

43:53.426 --> 43:57.227
- What?
- I'm so sorry if I'm wrong here...

43:57.293 --> 44:00.320
and I'm saying
something incredibly inappropriate.

44:00.393 --> 44:03.192
What?

44:03.259 --> 44:06.718
Did you put any of that in the food?

44:06.792 --> 44:09.023
- Yes. That would explain a lot.
- Lee asked me for some.

44:09.092 --> 44:10.583
Oh, come on, Amir.

44:10.659 --> 44:12.150
Are you serious?

44:12.226 --> 44:14.695
I had to ask.

44:14.759 --> 44:17.285
She asked to take some and I gave her some.

44:17.359 --> 44:19.555
When we did the mushrooms years ago...

44:19.625 --> 44:23.892
we talked about it,
and I put them in the spaghetti sauce.

44:23.959 --> 44:25.450
That was a group decision.

44:25.525 --> 44:27.426
I know we agreed, but I had to ask because-

44:27.492 --> 44:31.520
- You think that I would just
put drugs in your food?
- Oh, my God.

44:31.592 --> 44:33.493
Okay. I'll show you.

44:33.559 --> 44:35.528
On top of all this, you think I'd drug you?

44:35.592 --> 44:38.152
- I'll show you.
- Let's just see how much is in there.

44:38.226 --> 44:40.821
This is the vial I brought.

44:40.892 --> 44:42.383
Yeah, and a quarter of it is gone.

44:42.459 --> 44:45.122
But that's-She's had
a couple of drops out of it.

44:45.193 --> 44:48.095
- That's it.
- This is, like, high-grade pharmaceutical-

44:48.159 --> 44:50.151
- It is watered down.
- You can't.

44:50.226 --> 44:51.717
You opened it up and watered it down?

44:51.792 --> 44:53.351
Okay, but if you took enough of it...

44:53.426 --> 44:55.054
isn't it true that you
would have hallucinations?

44:55.126 --> 44:56.651
You would have to have a massive dose.

44:56.725 --> 44:58.523
You would have to take the entire bottle.

44:58.592 --> 45:00.083
Okay. Fine. But is it true?

45:01.859 --> 45:03.487
- Yes.
- Okay. And is it also true...

45:03.559 --> 45:05.824
that one of the other effects
can be paranoia?

45:05.892 --> 45:08.521
Yes, but you-

45:08.592 --> 45:10.857
- Again, you would have to have all of it.
- The whole bottle.

45:10.926 --> 45:12.417
- The whole bottle.
- And it would never-

45:12.492 --> 45:15.758
Even if all of us took a bottle each...

45:15.826 --> 45:18.091
it would never create a mass hallucination.

45:18.159 --> 45:21.721
- I'm not a criminal.
- It would be a nice conclusion right now.

45:21.792 --> 45:23.886
Wouldn't this be great if we were hallucinating?

45:23.959 --> 45:26.428
- Well, it's not the explanation.
- Fine.

45:26.492 --> 45:30.088
- I believe you. I asked for it.
- This is the bottle.

45:30.159 --> 45:32.321
- She asked for it. I gave her some.
- Okay.

45:32.393 --> 45:34.453
I-I did not drug your food.

45:34.525 --> 45:36.585
- I did not drug your food.
- I-

45:36.659 --> 45:39.151
- Get it?
- Lay off, okay?

45:39.226 --> 45:41.889
[Whispering ]
I swear to God.

45:41.959 --> 45:43.120
Thanks.

45:46.959 --> 45:49.224
Hey, where'd you get this? This is so cute.

45:49.293 --> 45:51.524
Oh, I got it at, uh, Galaxy. That thrift store.

45:51.592 --> 45:53.083
Oh, I love that place.

45:53.159 --> 45:54.991
- That's great.
- They have such cute stuff.

45:55.059 --> 45:57.551
I just- [Sighs]
I need a drink.

45:57.625 --> 45:59.150
[Chuckles]
Yeah.

45:59.226 --> 46:00.717
Okay.

46:02.126 --> 46:05.927
I just want to wake up
and start again, you know?

46:05.992 --> 46:07.688
[ Door Opening ]

46:07.759 --> 46:10.160
[ Hinges Squeak]

46:20.659 --> 46:22.423
Blue.

46:23.759 --> 46:25.352
It's not even cracked.

46:25.426 --> 46:27.622
[Whispering ]
What are we gonna do?

46:27.692 --> 46:29.684
We have to get the fuck out of here.

46:29.759 --> 46:31.489
Okay.

46:31.559 --> 46:33.187
- Okay. Let's take-
- Take the book.

46:33.259 --> 46:34.750
- Take the book.
- Do we take the box?

46:34.826 --> 46:38.024
- Take the box. This is what they-
- Take it.

46:38.092 --> 46:40.994
Hey. You okay?

46:41.892 --> 46:44.418
Where'd you go?

46:44.492 --> 46:46.085
I need a drink.

46:46.159 --> 46:50.096
Hey. What, uh-Where'd you go?

46:50.159 --> 46:51.718
I went to the house, dude.

46:51.792 --> 46:54.421
- I told you.
- What happened?

46:54.492 --> 46:56.518
I just dropped the letter off.

46:56.592 --> 47:00.688
Uh- I saw the book.

47:00.759 --> 47:04.355
I was gonna-
Uh, I was gonna smash the window...

47:04.426 --> 47:05.917
and take the book.

47:05.992 --> 47:08.393
I didn't do that, though. I did not do that.

47:08.459 --> 47:11.952
I just dropped off the letter, and, um-

47:12.026 --> 47:16.930
then I was gonna wait, to see their reaction.

47:16.992 --> 47:18.824
But I fuckin' freaked out.

47:18.892 --> 47:20.861
- You've been gone, like, five minutes.
- Like 45 minutes, dude.

47:20.926 --> 47:22.485
- No. No. You talked to me.
- Bullshit.

47:22.559 --> 47:24.050
You went in the kitchen.

47:24.126 --> 47:27.528
You've been gone for five, maybe 10 tops.

47:27.592 --> 47:29.584
You're fuckin' crazy.

47:31.725 --> 47:34.490
Oh, Mike. Mike, don't do that.

47:45.259 --> 47:47.285
- Oh, my God.
- Mike, what was-

47:47.359 --> 47:48.987
Don't do this.

47:49.059 --> 47:51.961
Mike, please? Why now?

47:52.026 --> 47:54.689
Why not now, honey? Why not now?

47:56.659 --> 47:58.924
- Where are Hugh and-
- We were in the kitchen.

47:58.992 --> 48:00.893
Where's-

48:00.959 --> 48:03.861
- Where's Hugh?
- Where's Amir?

48:03.926 --> 48:06.589
More importantly, where's the box?

48:06.659 --> 48:08.355
Oh, my God. They took the box.

48:08.426 --> 48:10.054
Mike, where did they go?

48:10.126 --> 48:12.789
- I have no clue where they went.
- You gotta be kidding.

48:12.859 --> 48:14.555
You were in here. What happened?

48:14.625 --> 48:18.027
Where's the book? Where's the book?

48:18.092 --> 48:21.221
Why would they bring that to the other house?

48:21.293 --> 48:24.559
They said they wanted to take it back
so they could make everything right.

48:24.625 --> 48:27.254
They wanted to return it, so everything
would be fine from the beginning, but-

48:27.326 --> 48:30.296
Why would they bring the book?
It's the one thing that we wouldn't-

48:30.359 --> 48:34.262
- They took everything we have.
- Wait a minute.

48:34.326 --> 48:35.817
We have to go get them.

48:35.892 --> 48:38.259
Wait a minute.
They were the first ones to leave, right?

48:38.326 --> 48:40.886
And then they-They came back.
They said they saw something.

48:40.959 --> 48:42.655
They've been acting weird ever since.

48:42.725 --> 48:46.685
- What are you implying?
- Oh, my God.

48:48.193 --> 48:50.389
- No, that's-Well, you guys left, too.
- Think about it.

48:50.459 --> 48:51.984
I mean, everyone-You left, too.

48:52.059 --> 48:53.721
- Amir came back and got so quiet...
- Come on.

48:53.792 --> 48:55.590
and then-and he didn't-

48:55.659 --> 48:57.560
- Amir was being totally weird.
- I'll bring 'em back.

48:57.625 --> 48:59.389
- I'll see what's going on.
- Baby, you're not-

48:59.459 --> 49:00.950
- You're not going anywhere.
- I'll be back.

49:01.026 --> 49:02.892
I'm just gonna go bring them back...

49:02.959 --> 49:04.450
and find out what the hell's going on.

49:04.525 --> 49:06.551
- No. You're not leaving.
- Baby, relax. What?

49:06.625 --> 49:08.116
- No.
- It's fine. I'll be back.

49:08.193 --> 49:11.595
I'm not gonna let you go.

49:12.826 --> 49:15.261
It would be fucking crazy.

49:21.426 --> 49:23.156
Okay. So, what are we gonna do?

49:23.226 --> 49:26.424
I mean, they're out there, and I swear to God,
I'm gonna have a heart attack.

49:26.492 --> 49:28.256
- We've gotta do something.
- Let's have a drink.

49:28.326 --> 49:29.988
We don't even know if that was them.

49:30.059 --> 49:31.994
Would you quit saying that, please?

49:32.059 --> 49:33.960
No, but if it wasn't them, then Mike is right...

49:34.026 --> 49:35.585
and we can't trust the other house.

49:35.659 --> 49:37.184
- We can't trust ourselves.
- That's right.

49:37.259 --> 49:40.718
- Jesus.
- And our clues just left the house.

49:43.926 --> 49:46.794
No. Wait.

49:46.859 --> 49:50.523
The clues are still here.

49:50.592 --> 49:53.084
If they had the pictures, then-

49:53.159 --> 49:55.492
Mike, you took that picture
of me and Kevin. Right?

49:55.559 --> 49:58.358
Do you have it here?

49:58.426 --> 50:01.521
I-I can't take this anymore.
I can't take it.

50:01.592 --> 50:03.891
- Sweetheart-
- Can you at least go look for it?

50:06.426 --> 50:08.895
I'm gonna look for another bottle of wine.

50:25.992 --> 50:27.756
This is so stupid.

50:28.992 --> 50:30.654
Should I be keeping an eye on him?

50:30.725 --> 50:33.786
I feel like I don't want to hover, and-

50:33.859 --> 50:36.590
I don't know.

50:38.859 --> 50:40.919
Just give it a minute, and then-

50:42.959 --> 50:44.552
go in and talk to him, I guess.

50:47.326 --> 50:50.888
I don't know who Mike is anymore.
Not when he drinks.

50:50.959 --> 50:53.656
Everything that's gone wrong
with us started when he started drinking.

50:53.725 --> 50:55.353
It's why we had to leave L.A.

50:55.426 --> 50:57.258
It's why he doesn't have a career.

50:57.326 --> 50:59.818
He's just- I don't know.

50:59.892 --> 51:01.884
Not the man I married.

51:59.692 --> 52:01.684
[Sighs]

52:03.625 --> 52:05.321
Hey.

52:05.393 --> 52:07.453
- Hey.
- How you doing?

52:07.525 --> 52:09.892
How you holding up?

52:09.959 --> 52:12.190
All things considered, all right.

52:12.259 --> 52:14.694
[Chuckling ] I totally
don't believe you.

52:14.759 --> 52:16.728
- Yeah. Well, am I being some-
- What's going on?

52:16.792 --> 52:18.556
I- Amir told me
you were gonna go to Vietnam...

52:18.625 --> 52:20.116
and Em's not going with you?

52:20.193 --> 52:22.025
Yeah. I, uh-

52:22.092 --> 52:23.890
I gotta go for work for, I don't know-

52:23.959 --> 52:26.155
It's four months, I think, and, uh...

52:26.226 --> 52:28.252
yeah, I want her to come along, but, uh-

52:28.326 --> 52:29.851
She'd be crazy not to go with you.

52:29.926 --> 52:31.895
[Chuckling ]
Yeah. That's what I think.

52:31.959 --> 52:33.655
Yeah. I don't- I don't know.

52:33.725 --> 52:35.887
I mean, it's-
I-I really don't want to interfere.

52:35.959 --> 52:37.450
It doesn't seem like any of my business...

52:37.525 --> 52:40.188
but I think you've always
been someone...

52:40.259 --> 52:43.491
who's extremely passionate
about your life and what you're doing...

52:43.559 --> 52:46.393
and if you have a partner
that seems to hesitate all the time...

52:46.459 --> 52:50.726
with things of life,
I don't know if that's gonna make you happy.

52:50.792 --> 52:53.159
Oh. She's, uh-

52:53.226 --> 52:55.855
I mean, I love her, and- It's just who she is.

52:55.926 --> 52:58.657
- Sometimes she's a little-
- Tall?

53:01.625 --> 53:03.594
- Crazy.
- She's a little bit tall.

53:03.659 --> 53:05.924
I mean, do you have
to stand on your tiptoes to kiss her?

53:05.992 --> 53:08.052
- I-
- [ Laughing ]

53:11.826 --> 53:14.057
Sometimes people just fit well.

53:14.126 --> 53:17.096
- Laurie-
- Like that Sharks game?

53:17.159 --> 53:20.220
Come on, you can't tell me we don't fit well.

53:20.293 --> 53:22.922
I had to do yoga
for a week afterwards to recover.

53:22.992 --> 53:25.985
- [ Both Chuckling ]
- I do remember that.

53:26.059 --> 53:29.188
I just think that maybe-

53:33.926 --> 53:35.758
Laurie.

53:35.826 --> 53:39.627
- I'm sorry. I'm crossing all kinds
of boundaries with you.
- Yeah.

53:45.692 --> 53:47.251
[Sighs]

53:50.226 --> 53:53.219
- Baby?
- Hi.

53:53.293 --> 53:56.752
You know, I think you're right...

53:56.826 --> 53:59.887
that everything happens for a reason.

54:01.059 --> 54:02.721
[ Audible Exhale]

54:06.625 --> 54:09.561
Should I get the bat?

54:09.625 --> 54:11.856
For you or for me?

54:11.926 --> 54:13.827
Could be either.
[Chuckles]

54:16.459 --> 54:18.758
What are we doing here?

54:18.826 --> 54:24.857
If I'm losing it over there, I'm losing it here.

54:24.926 --> 54:27.259
- Ah, it doesn't have to be like that.
- Sure, it does.

54:27.326 --> 54:29.386
It's the same thing.

54:29.459 --> 54:31.724
No, it's not.

54:31.792 --> 54:34.421
How do you figure?

54:34.492 --> 54:39.294
Because there's no way that anybody
over there, or- or anywhere...

54:39.359 --> 54:43.023
loves you as much as I love you right here.

54:49.193 --> 54:52.425
I fucked up.

55:01.625 --> 55:04.254
- Hi.
- Hey.

55:04.326 --> 55:08.058
How you doing?

55:08.126 --> 55:11.494
Uh, fine.

55:12.659 --> 55:15.424
Is- Is everything okay?

55:15.492 --> 55:18.326
Is there something going on?

55:19.759 --> 55:23.992
Beth just walked up to me and, uh-

55:24.059 --> 55:28.292
she didn't really say much,
but she said that she...

55:28.359 --> 55:31.693
saw you and Laurie talk in the hallway, and-

55:32.659 --> 55:34.287
Jesus Christ, Em. I think we have...

55:34.359 --> 55:36.385
some more important things
to worry about right now...

55:36.459 --> 55:38.724
than what Beth is saying.

55:42.725 --> 55:44.921
- [ Loud Report, Crackling ]
- Jesus Christ.

55:44.992 --> 55:47.120
- Are you kidding me?
- That would be the generator.

55:47.193 --> 55:49.719
- Hold on.
- All right. You know what to do.

55:49.792 --> 55:51.818
- We have thousands of matches at home.
- Don't burn yourself.

55:51.892 --> 55:54.191
- Kevin, do you have matches?
- Yeah, I got some.

55:54.259 --> 55:56.319
Here.

55:56.393 --> 55:58.021
- Hold it.
- I don't know-

55:58.092 --> 56:00.152
- You want to put this on the table?
- Yeah. Yeah.

56:00.226 --> 56:02.422
- [ Report, Crackling ]
- That was right out front.

56:02.492 --> 56:04.688
- Are you kidding?
- That sounds like one of our cars.

56:04.759 --> 56:06.318
Like one of our cars getting broken into.

56:06.393 --> 56:08.089
Look, I'm going out there. I can't stand this.

56:08.159 --> 56:10.390
- I'm gonna go see what's going on.
- Not without the rest of us.

56:10.459 --> 56:13.327
- Let's just all go.
- Fine. Then let's all go, but I'm going.

56:13.393 --> 56:15.021
- I'll get my coat.
- I don't think we should.

56:15.092 --> 56:16.822
- Let's get a flashlight.
- We'll be fine.

56:16.892 --> 56:18.724
- Here. I got one here.
- You guys lead, okay?

56:18.792 --> 56:20.317
- You ready?
- Okay. Here we go.

56:20.393 --> 56:22.089
- Stay close. Stay close.
- Here we go.

56:22.159 --> 56:24.856
- Where did it come from?
- I don't know.

56:29.892 --> 56:31.451
That's it, right?

56:33.725 --> 56:36.388
- Oh, my God.
- Jesus. Look.

56:37.659 --> 56:41.619
- Is there anything in there?
- I don't see anything.

56:41.692 --> 56:44.093
Oh, my God. Should we-

56:44.159 --> 56:46.185
- Should we check our cars?
- That's crazy.

56:46.259 --> 56:47.852
Yeah, why doesn't everybody
check their own car.

56:47.926 --> 56:49.895
- See if we find anything else.
- Let's look at our cars.

56:49.959 --> 56:52.326
- Okay.
- All right. After you.

56:52.393 --> 56:55.659
Is everyone nearby?

56:55.725 --> 56:58.627
We shouldn't spread out too much.

56:59.625 --> 57:01.253
[Car Chirps Twice]

57:13.625 --> 57:16.390
- [ Knocking ]
- [Gasps, Audible Exhale]

57:16.459 --> 57:18.758
- Hey.
- Everything okay?

57:18.826 --> 57:22.319
Yeah. I just-

57:22.393 --> 57:27.331
put this ring on
that you got me at the fair.

57:27.393 --> 57:29.658
Remember? I know it's-

57:29.725 --> 57:32.388
I know it's cheesy,
but I just wanted to have it on.

57:32.459 --> 57:34.587
Cheeseball.

57:34.659 --> 57:38.824
- It was a good day.
- It was a good day.

57:38.892 --> 57:41.088
Are we okay?

57:41.159 --> 57:45.221
- Yeah, babe.
- After that whole Laurie thing?

57:45.293 --> 57:47.285
Uh, yeah.

57:47.359 --> 57:49.157
I don't know what the hell
she's thinking...

57:49.226 --> 57:52.219
but yeah, we're good.

57:52.293 --> 57:55.422
Come here. Hey.

58:00.026 --> 58:02.552
Is everything okay with Hugh's car?

58:02.625 --> 58:07.359
- What do you mean?
- Well, did they take anything?

58:07.426 --> 58:10.362
You just checked on his car.
Did they take anything?

58:39.359 --> 58:41.385
Doesn't make any sense at all.

58:41.459 --> 58:43.951
Do you think it's just someone
trying to intimidate us?

58:44.026 --> 58:45.585
Intimidate? No. I- It's-

58:45.659 --> 58:47.890
None of this- It doesn't-

58:47.959 --> 58:51.088
I mean, it's like they're
looking for something, and-

58:51.159 --> 58:54.254
- But there's nothing in there.
- Exactly. There's nothing in there. So, why-

58:54.326 --> 58:55.817
They could see that there's nothing in there.

58:55.892 --> 58:57.827
- We could see that there's nothing in there.
- I know.

58:57.892 --> 59:00.259
Why break the window if there's nothing there?

59:00.326 --> 59:03.694
- That doesn't make any sense.
- None of this makes any sense.

59:03.759 --> 59:05.318
Where were you?

59:05.393 --> 59:08.727
I went and got this ring.

59:08.792 --> 59:11.626
Nice.

59:12.892 --> 59:14.724
All right, hold on. Let's-Let's-

59:14.792 --> 59:17.660
Let's just try and figure out...

59:17.725 --> 59:23.665
why we would break into a car-
Hugh's car-

59:23.725 --> 59:25.853
knowing that the book wasn't there.

59:25.926 --> 59:27.918
[ Laurie] Well, we're assuming
that the book is the motive.

59:27.992 --> 59:30.757
What if the motive is completely different?

59:30.826 --> 59:32.692
- Did you hear something?
- What the hell is that?

59:32.759 --> 59:34.387
- It's outside.
- No, Mike, Mike, Mike, Mike.

59:34.459 --> 59:37.918
- Oh, shit! There's someone coming.
- What?

59:37.992 --> 59:40.052
They're coming over here, guys.

59:40.126 --> 59:41.822
Yeah. It's Hugh.

59:41.892 --> 59:43.793
- Is it Hugh?
- Is it Hugh and Amir?

59:43.859 --> 59:46.385
Yeah, it's blue. It's Hugh and Amir. Cool.

59:46.459 --> 59:48.894
- They're coming to the door.
- Are you sure?

59:48.959 --> 59:52.157
- It looks like it.
- Oh, baby.

59:52.226 --> 59:53.990
- [ Laughing ]
- Are you all okay?

59:54.059 --> 59:57.257
- Hey, where have you been? What happened?
- Okay.

59:57.326 --> 01:00:00.592
What have you been-
Why did you take-What did you do?

01:00:00.659 --> 01:00:03.652
- Can you please tell us what happened?
- We went to, uh-

01:00:03.725 --> 01:00:06.695
We went to make a phone call,
and then when, uh-

01:00:06.759 --> 01:00:08.591
when we looked in the door, we saw-

01:00:08.659 --> 01:00:12.858
We saw this, basically. I, uh, I got startled.

01:00:12.926 --> 01:00:15.452
I fell over. I hit my head.
We went back to the house to-

01:00:15.525 --> 01:00:17.687
- [Chattering ]
- Wait. You already came back here.

01:00:17.759 --> 01:00:19.387
We already heard this story.

01:00:19.459 --> 01:00:21.155
Why are you telling us this story again?

01:00:21.226 --> 01:00:22.854
- You came back with the box.
- Wait. What?

01:00:22.926 --> 01:00:24.918
Because you came back,
and after you hit your head-

01:00:24.992 --> 01:00:29.930
- We gave him a Band-Aid and you gave us the-
- But not that Band-Aid.

01:00:29.992 --> 01:00:33.690
- What do you mean?
- Oh, my God. I gave you a cloth Band-Aid.

01:00:33.759 --> 01:00:36.991
Wait a minute. Hugh-
There was a Hugh and an Amir here?

01:00:37.059 --> 01:00:38.960
Yes. And you left with the book.

01:00:39.026 --> 01:00:41.689
You left with the pictures,
and we didn't know where you went.

01:00:41.759 --> 01:00:44.160
We were at a house where
everybody had red glow sticks.

01:00:44.226 --> 01:00:46.821
- You had red glow sticks.
- Do you understand?

01:00:46.892 --> 01:00:50.761
We-We have red glow-
We took them from the other house.

01:00:50.826 --> 01:00:52.954
- Right.
- Look. Look.

01:00:53.026 --> 01:00:56.087
Is that- Look. That box
of red glow sticks is unopened.

01:00:56.159 --> 01:00:59.323
Guys, if they started here, they belong here.

01:00:59.393 --> 01:01:01.555
They're in the right house.

01:01:01.625 --> 01:01:04.356
- Well, welcome back.
- Welcome back.

01:01:04.426 --> 01:01:06.986
- Jeez, man, I'm sorry.
- That's all right.

01:01:07.059 --> 01:01:09.085
- Huh?
- Sorry.

01:01:09.159 --> 01:01:13.187
So, guys, what was the other Mike like?
What was he doing?

01:01:13.259 --> 01:01:17.094
The other Mike is, uh- He's worried about you.

01:01:18.792 --> 01:01:20.761
So, it was you guys who left us the note.

01:01:20.826 --> 01:01:24.354
No, I never got out with that note.

01:01:24.426 --> 01:01:26.224
We ended up with two notes.

01:01:26.293 --> 01:01:28.159
And so did we.

01:01:28.226 --> 01:01:30.092
- Well, where's-
- We have two notes.

01:01:30.159 --> 01:01:34.358
One that was written here and
one that was left on the door.

01:01:34.426 --> 01:01:37.760
If you didn't, and if the other Hugh didn't...

01:01:37.826 --> 01:01:40.921
then who has been leaving the notes?

01:01:40.992 --> 01:01:44.121
"Quantum decoherence ensures
that the different outcomes...

01:01:44.193 --> 01:01:46.492
have no interaction with one another."

01:01:46.559 --> 01:01:49.222
So, that one note has been
written at least four times.

01:01:49.293 --> 01:01:51.956
Well, how many Hugh and Amirs
are walking around out there?

01:01:54.992 --> 01:01:56.517
Okay, before we do anything...

01:01:56.592 --> 01:01:59.585
we have to figure out
how to mark our own house.

01:01:59.659 --> 01:02:02.060
- Just stay inside.
- No, no. She's right.

01:02:02.126 --> 01:02:04.561
Staying inside isn't realistic.

01:02:04.625 --> 01:02:07.686
We need some kind of marker.
We got to mark this house.

01:02:07.759 --> 01:02:09.250
If every house is the same-

01:02:09.326 --> 01:02:11.318
If we put a marker in front of the house...

01:02:11.393 --> 01:02:13.487
there could be an infinite number of
houses with that mark.

01:02:13.559 --> 01:02:15.187
So, we have to do something random.

01:02:15.259 --> 01:02:16.852
Something that can't be repeated.
Something unique.

01:02:16.926 --> 01:02:19.122
Dice. Do we have dice?
We have dice?

01:02:19.193 --> 01:02:23.187
- Um, Yahtzee.
- Yeah, Yahtzee.

01:02:23.259 --> 01:02:27.287
If we each roll a number for each of us,
that's what? That's-

01:02:27.359 --> 01:02:30.329
Six times six times six times six times-
That's hugely random.

01:02:30.393 --> 01:02:33.921
- The probability of that repeating is-tiny.
- And then what? We-

01:02:33.992 --> 01:02:36.587
But so we have to have something visual.

01:02:36.659 --> 01:02:40.494
I mean, should we write it down, put it in- put
it outside? Put it in an envelope?

01:02:40.559 --> 01:02:42.050
- We still won't know.
- No, no, no, no.

01:02:42.126 --> 01:02:43.651
We need something to mark it.

01:02:43.725 --> 01:02:47.025
Yeah. We put it in a box.

01:02:47.092 --> 01:02:49.061
- That's, that's-
- That's exactly what they've done.

01:02:49.126 --> 01:02:51.721
- They were ahead of us.
- They were making a marker for their house.

01:02:51.792 --> 01:02:54.023
They made a unique mark.
Only we took it.

01:02:54.092 --> 01:02:55.958
If it seems like a good idea to us...

01:02:56.026 --> 01:02:57.585
it would seem like a good idea to them.

01:02:57.659 --> 01:03:00.754
- Do you have a box?
- Yeah. Yeah, let me look.

01:03:00.826 --> 01:03:02.692
So, we need photos.

01:03:02.759 --> 01:03:05.524
- This is so crazy.
- It's par for the night.

01:03:05.592 --> 01:03:07.925
- There are a lot of pictures here.
- You can't use that picture.

01:03:07.992 --> 01:03:09.961
That's ridiculous.

01:03:10.026 --> 01:03:13.224
- I'm the attorney for Grizzly Adams.
- Yeah, I know. This is-

01:03:13.293 --> 01:03:14.989
I'm never hiring you.

01:03:15.059 --> 01:03:17.961
How does this work as a box?

01:03:18.026 --> 01:03:19.756
I didn't even know we had it.

01:03:19.826 --> 01:03:22.261
It was just under a pile of crap in the back.

01:03:22.326 --> 01:03:23.988
- If you can-
- That'll work.

01:03:24.059 --> 01:03:26.221
So, tha-Tha-That's your box?

01:03:26.293 --> 01:03:29.388
- It was here all the time.
- Of course it was.

01:03:29.459 --> 01:03:33.021
I'm not too happy about cutting these pictures.

01:03:33.092 --> 01:03:35.493
And we only have pictures of you
and I together, babe.

01:03:35.559 --> 01:03:38.996
I actually- I actually have a photo of Kevin.

01:03:39.059 --> 01:03:41.028
- I know that's strange. Um-
- What?

01:03:41.092 --> 01:03:43.994
No, I have my, um-

01:03:44.059 --> 01:03:47.518
My checking account number is written on the
back of this old photo that I have...

01:03:47.592 --> 01:03:49.686
and it's just been in my wallet forever.

01:03:49.759 --> 01:03:51.421
- It's right here.
- Mmm.

01:03:51.492 --> 01:03:54.087
- What?
- You know what? I-I'll just-

01:03:54.159 --> 01:03:57.152
- I'll cut this picture that we have here.
- Just use this one. It's okay.

01:03:57.226 --> 01:04:00.560
- Just scratch off the number.
- Cut.

01:04:00.625 --> 01:04:02.890
Great. I think we got one
of everybody except me, so-

01:04:02.959 --> 01:04:06.259
I'm glad you guys all keep a lot of pictures
of your friend, Amir.

01:04:06.326 --> 01:04:10.161
- Well, we'll take one of you.
- [Whirring ]

01:04:10.226 --> 01:04:12.161
Smile, dickhead.

01:04:12.226 --> 01:04:14.388
[ Beeps]

01:04:14.459 --> 01:04:15.950
- [Chirps]
- Let me see.

01:04:16.026 --> 01:04:17.517
It's not exactly the same.

01:04:17.592 --> 01:04:20.460
It's not the same as the one from the other box.

01:04:20.525 --> 01:04:24.018
They took a picture of me in the other house,
but it's not exactly the same.

01:04:24.092 --> 01:04:27.324
This is what we're talking about.
That's a moment where it can be...

01:04:27.393 --> 01:04:28.918
a different-a divergent moment.

01:04:28.992 --> 01:04:31.154
That's what we're gonna do
right now with these dice.

01:04:31.226 --> 01:04:33.024
Wait. Since we're the blue house...

01:04:33.092 --> 01:04:34.583
shouldn't we use a blue pen?

01:04:34.659 --> 01:04:36.457
- Just to make it even more-
- That makes sense.

01:04:36.525 --> 01:04:38.653
- Yeah?
- The odds go up by three.

01:04:38.725 --> 01:04:40.819
So, does everyone have a die?

01:04:40.892 --> 01:04:42.417
- What's yours?
- Beth?

01:04:42.492 --> 01:04:44.688
All right.

01:04:44.759 --> 01:04:47.752
Six.

01:04:47.826 --> 01:04:50.091
- Hugh?
- Three.

01:04:50.159 --> 01:04:52.390
- Mike?
- Four.

01:04:52.459 --> 01:04:54.360
- [ Die Rattles]
- Six.

01:04:54.426 --> 01:04:57.294
- [ Die Rattles]
- Two.

01:04:57.359 --> 01:04:59.726
You guys know what a quick code is?
You know when you...

01:04:59.792 --> 01:05:01.761
are going online,
going into your bank account...

01:05:01.826 --> 01:05:03.727
and when you go to your password,
it'll give you...

01:05:03.792 --> 01:05:05.693
a picture to choose?

01:05:05.759 --> 01:05:09.696
That's your quick code. That's called an MFA.
It's a multi-factor authenticator.

01:05:09.759 --> 01:05:12.285
We do 'em. We put 'em in
whenever we build our big sites.

01:05:12.359 --> 01:05:13.884
It's an icon, right?

01:05:13.959 --> 01:05:17.054
- Sort of a random-
- A random object.

01:05:17.126 --> 01:05:18.890
Yeah. So, what if each of these...

01:05:18.959 --> 01:05:22.396
has a random object in it
to sort of serve as that quick code, right?

01:05:22.459 --> 01:05:24.655
Right. Right.
So, we pick something to put in there.

01:05:24.725 --> 01:05:28.253
You could put anything
in there, right? A candle or a book or, um-

01:05:28.326 --> 01:05:30.921
- The oven mitt.
- Or a ping-pong paddle.

01:05:30.992 --> 01:05:33.723
Or a ping-pong paddle. Exactly. Yeah.

01:05:33.792 --> 01:05:37.229
Exactly.

01:05:37.293 --> 01:05:40.161
- Well, how's this? And this is random, right?
- A coaster?

01:05:40.226 --> 01:05:42.286
Is anything really random tonight?

01:05:42.359 --> 01:05:43.850
If you have to leave...

01:05:43.926 --> 01:05:45.417
when you check the box, open it up...

01:05:45.492 --> 01:05:47.518
you see that,
you know you're off to a good start.

01:05:47.592 --> 01:05:49.220
- [Sighs]
- I feel better.

01:05:49.293 --> 01:05:50.886
Okay. So we've got the box.

01:05:50.959 --> 01:05:53.224
Yeah, and it only
took all night to figure it out.

01:05:53.293 --> 01:05:54.886
We've marked the house. If we stay together...

01:05:54.959 --> 01:05:59.226
keep our heads up, and nobody
wanders off, we can get through this.

01:05:59.293 --> 01:06:00.852
- Thanks, coach.
- Yeah.

01:06:00.926 --> 01:06:03.828
- You want something?
- Yeah, water. Water would be great.

01:06:03.892 --> 01:06:06.088
I'm gonna get a drink.

01:06:06.159 --> 01:06:08.560
I wonder how different those
numbers are from the first box?

01:06:10.159 --> 01:06:11.957
Let me check.

01:06:12.026 --> 01:06:14.222
Where's my calculator?

01:06:14.293 --> 01:06:19.391
Let's see. So, if there's eight of us-

01:06:19.459 --> 01:06:23.362
and it's six times six...

01:06:23.426 --> 01:06:25.861
times six.

01:06:25.926 --> 01:06:31.490
Three different
colored glow sticks times three...

01:06:31.559 --> 01:06:37.260
is 5,038,848 possible variables.

01:06:37.326 --> 01:06:39.886
So, that's the variable.

01:06:47.126 --> 01:06:49.561
- Are you okay?
- Mm-hmm.

01:06:54.126 --> 01:06:56.357
[Sighs]

01:06:58.792 --> 01:07:00.727
Everything okay with the numbers?

01:07:00.792 --> 01:07:02.556
Yeah.

01:07:02.625 --> 01:07:07.359
D-Do you remember what number was written
on the back of your picture?

01:07:07.426 --> 01:07:09.588
- Five. Mm-hmm.
- Yeah?

01:07:09.659 --> 01:07:13.562
I found a good spot out front, just as long as
another Hugh and Amir don't come by.

01:07:13.625 --> 01:07:16.254
Kevin, do you remember what number
was written on the back of your picture?

01:07:16.326 --> 01:07:19.819
- Uh, six.
- Yeah?

01:07:19.892 --> 01:07:23.226
- Beth?
- Uh, three.

01:07:23.293 --> 01:07:24.818
Hugh, do you remember?

01:07:24.892 --> 01:07:26.986
- I was a three.
- You sure?

01:07:27.059 --> 01:07:30.962
Yeah. What's going on in the kitchen?

01:07:31.026 --> 01:07:33.188
- Pound cake.
- Pound cake.

01:07:33.259 --> 01:07:35.819
The girls are breaking out dessert...

01:07:35.892 --> 01:07:38.521
before the other house eats it.

01:07:42.592 --> 01:07:44.390
Hey, Mike, I need to show you something.

01:07:48.092 --> 01:07:50.584
The numbers that I remember...

01:07:50.659 --> 01:07:54.061
from the box that was brought
here from the other house...

01:07:54.126 --> 01:07:56.186
are these numbers.

01:07:58.459 --> 01:08:01.725
But these are the numbers that I found here...

01:08:01.792 --> 01:08:04.819
in this notepad.

01:08:04.892 --> 01:08:08.351
And I just asked everyone if
they can remember their number.

01:08:08.426 --> 01:08:11.692
Beth and Lee are from this house originally...

01:08:11.759 --> 01:08:15.059
because they have never left.

01:08:15.126 --> 01:08:19.496
But the rest of us-We are not from this house.

01:08:19.559 --> 01:08:21.994
We are visitors.

01:08:22.059 --> 01:08:24.494
Which means that this Lee is not your wife.

01:08:26.725 --> 01:08:29.456
- Are you with me?
- [Chuckling ]

01:08:33.159 --> 01:08:36.061
- Well, there's more.
- [Chuckling Continues]

01:08:36.126 --> 01:08:39.528
- Because Hugh and Amir...
- Hmm?

01:08:39.592 --> 01:08:41.823
are from a third house.

01:08:41.892 --> 01:08:46.023
He just showed me his phone. It's not cracked.

01:08:47.226 --> 01:08:50.162
Remember that dark area
that we walked through?

01:08:50.226 --> 01:08:52.661
I have a feeling that whoever
walks through that...

01:08:52.725 --> 01:08:56.218
is like they end up in the middle
of a roulette wheel...

01:08:56.293 --> 01:08:59.559
and they will just end up somewhere by chance.

01:08:59.625 --> 01:09:01.560
And whoever walks through there...

01:09:01.625 --> 01:09:04.595
will not return to the house
that they just left.

01:09:07.226 --> 01:09:11.288
And I think that we need to find our way back to
our house before the comet passes...

01:09:11.359 --> 01:09:13.726
because we- once it- once it passes...

01:09:13.792 --> 01:09:15.761
we might just be stuck exact- here.

01:09:15.826 --> 01:09:17.590
Wherever we are.

01:09:19.059 --> 01:09:22.757
I don't want to be stuck here.

01:09:22.826 --> 01:09:25.022
If your theory is true-

01:09:25.092 --> 01:09:26.754
If we walk through the dark space...

01:09:26.826 --> 01:09:28.317
and it is a roulette wheel...

01:09:28.393 --> 01:09:30.453
there's no way we can be sure...

01:09:30.525 --> 01:09:35.429
that we would go back to our original house.

01:09:35.492 --> 01:09:38.052
I think we just stay here.

01:09:38.126 --> 01:09:39.890
I think we're stuck here.

01:09:41.259 --> 01:09:43.785
I put it out near the gate. Should be all right.

01:09:43.859 --> 01:09:47.159
- If we all stay here, we should be okay.
- [Clattering ]

01:09:47.226 --> 01:09:49.092
Don't open it.

01:09:49.159 --> 01:09:51.253
Who is that?

01:09:52.792 --> 01:09:54.454
Oh.

01:09:54.525 --> 01:09:57.017
- What is it?
- Mike.

01:09:57.092 --> 01:10:00.358
- Oh, fuck me.
- Oh, jeez.

01:10:00.426 --> 01:10:02.054
- "Mike, my friend...
- [ Em ] What is it?

01:10:02.126 --> 01:10:05.426
Beth plus book equals Trinidad Club.

01:10:05.492 --> 01:10:07.427
Don't let it happen, whatever it takes, buddy."

01:10:07.492 --> 01:10:09.893
What is this?

01:10:09.959 --> 01:10:11.951
It's just this note. It's- Mike had this-

01:10:12.026 --> 01:10:15.053
He had this crazy idea
that maybe if he left this note out there...

01:10:15.126 --> 01:10:16.617
it could stop them getting the book.

01:10:16.692 --> 01:10:18.183
It's nothing. It was a stupid idea.

01:10:18.259 --> 01:10:20.387
But our Mike didn't deliver it.
What is this?

01:10:20.459 --> 01:10:22.291
Just some crazy other Mike running around.
It's nothing.

01:10:22.359 --> 01:10:24.692
- You know what it is? What is this?
- We talked about it.

01:10:24.759 --> 01:10:26.250
- What is it?
- Really, it's nothing.

01:10:26.326 --> 01:10:28.386
- Just let it go, and-
- Then why can't you tell us?

01:10:28.459 --> 01:10:30.951
Huh? Beth?

01:10:35.159 --> 01:10:37.754
- Mike, what is this?
- Oh, shit.

01:10:37.826 --> 01:10:40.591
It's-

01:10:40.659 --> 01:10:42.184
Nothing.

01:10:42.259 --> 01:10:44.194
If it's nothing, then why does my wife...

01:10:44.259 --> 01:10:45.887
have a fucking nosebleed?

01:10:45.959 --> 01:10:48.986
- Oh.
- Oh, honey. Oh, God. Oh, God.

01:10:49.059 --> 01:10:51.085
- Beth, what the hell is this?
- I told you.

01:10:51.159 --> 01:10:53.185
- I told you this was the worst.
- What is the idea?

01:10:53.259 --> 01:10:55.353
12 years ago. Mike and Beth.

01:10:55.426 --> 01:10:57.292
- You've gotta be kidding me.
- He was gonna blackmail himself...

01:10:57.359 --> 01:11:01.490
- What is this?
- so they would not get the book.

01:11:01.559 --> 01:11:03.551
This is bad. This is really bad.

01:11:03.625 --> 01:11:07.426
- Wait. You never told Hugh?
- It was on my to-do list.

01:11:07.492 --> 01:11:09.654
We have to just get through the night, okay?

01:11:09.725 --> 01:11:12.786
- Let's just try.
- [ Beth ] He told you.
He said he told you about it.

01:11:12.859 --> 01:11:14.350
[ Hugh ] Why didn't you
tell me?

01:11:14.426 --> 01:11:18.227
- Because you didn't say anything about it.
- Who else knew about this?

01:11:18.293 --> 01:11:20.125
Who else knew about this?

01:11:20.193 --> 01:11:22.719
- Lee, did you know about this?
- Yes.

01:11:22.792 --> 01:11:25.762
- Kevin, did you know?
- He told us. He told you. He-

01:11:25.826 --> 01:11:28.261
- Everybody knew about this.
- We thought you knew.

01:11:28.326 --> 01:11:30.693
Everybody knew
about this except me?

01:11:30.759 --> 01:11:35.697
Hugh, listen. It's-
It's not what it seems. It's-

01:11:35.759 --> 01:11:39.855
- We don't even belong here.
- You are fucking too much, man.

01:11:39.926 --> 01:11:42.555
- You are fucking too much.
- Listen. We're visitors here.

01:11:42.625 --> 01:11:44.560
- This isn't our house.
- What are you talking about?

01:11:44.625 --> 01:11:46.150
This is Lee and Beth's house.

01:11:46.226 --> 01:11:49.321
You sleep with my wife,
and this is what you're telling me?

01:11:49.393 --> 01:11:50.884
Check your phone. Is your phone broken?

01:11:50.959 --> 01:11:52.951
What the fuck does that
have to do with anything?

01:11:53.026 --> 01:11:56.224
- Is your phone broken?
- What the fuck does that
have to do with anything?

01:11:56.293 --> 01:11:59.127
- Just do it.
- Show us.

01:11:59.193 --> 01:12:00.752
No. My phone is not broken.

01:12:00.826 --> 01:12:03.421
Now what does that have to do
with you sleeping with my wife?

01:12:03.492 --> 01:12:06.257
From the beginning of the evening,
your phone was broken.

01:12:06.326 --> 01:12:08.591
- [ Hugh ] No. Em's phone is broken.
- So is yours.

01:12:08.659 --> 01:12:11.390
Your-The box.
The first box that we got...

01:12:11.459 --> 01:12:13.257
we had, uh, like, a random item.

01:12:13.326 --> 01:12:14.919
W-What w-was your random item?

01:12:14.992 --> 01:12:16.893
What the fuck does
this have to do with anything?

01:12:16.959 --> 01:12:19.053
Answer him.

01:12:19.126 --> 01:12:22.528
- The stapler.
- No, no, no.

01:12:22.592 --> 01:12:24.117
- What?
- We had an oven mitt.

01:12:24.193 --> 01:12:26.287
And ours was a ping-pong paddle.

01:12:26.359 --> 01:12:28.658
- What?
- Mine was a napkin.

01:12:28.725 --> 01:12:30.819
What the fuck are you talking about?

01:12:30.892 --> 01:12:34.795
Hugh, that is not my Lee.
That is not your Beth, and I am not your Mike.

01:12:34.859 --> 01:12:36.851
You-You aren't mad at me.

01:12:36.926 --> 01:12:39.657
W-We're in a different-
a different reality here.

01:12:39.725 --> 01:12:42.820
Yeah, we're in a different
reality because the reality where I am from...

01:12:42.892 --> 01:12:45.293
my best friend
didn't sleep with my wife.

01:12:45.359 --> 01:12:48.261
Hugh, do you not understand what I'm saying?

01:12:48.326 --> 01:12:53.094
This all started tonight, and if there are
a million different realities...

01:12:53.159 --> 01:12:55.822
I have slept with your wife
in every one of them.

01:12:55.892 --> 01:12:59.158
- You fucking-
- No, no, no.

01:12:59.226 --> 01:13:02.219
- Hugh! Hugh!
- [ All Yelling ]

01:13:03.226 --> 01:13:05.354
Come on!

01:13:05.426 --> 01:13:07.395
- Are you okay?
- Yeah. Settle down.

01:13:07.459 --> 01:13:09.553
I'm gonna get some ice.
I'm gonna get some ice.

01:13:09.625 --> 01:13:11.856
[ Panting ]

01:13:11.926 --> 01:13:14.054
Are you okay?

01:13:15.293 --> 01:13:17.853
Sit down.

01:13:18.992 --> 01:13:20.654
You okay, baby?

01:13:20.725 --> 01:13:22.956
- Here, let me give you a little of this.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:13:23.026 --> 01:13:25.757
Okay, I'm going to put
something on it. I'll put something on it.

01:13:28.259 --> 01:13:32.321
You know, I've made some-some choices, uh,
that I'm stuck with. Um-

01:13:32.393 --> 01:13:36.262
I'm stuck here.

01:13:36.326 --> 01:13:38.056
[ Audible Inhale, Exhale]

01:13:38.126 --> 01:13:41.255
I'm like the dead cat,
right?

01:13:41.326 --> 01:13:42.919
This whole night we've been worrying...

01:13:42.992 --> 01:13:48.260
there's some dark version of us
out there somewhere.

01:13:48.326 --> 01:13:50.386
What if we're the dark version?

01:13:51.959 --> 01:13:53.951
- What's that?
- [Sobbing ]

01:13:54.026 --> 01:13:55.995
- All right.
- [ Hugh ] Goddamn it!

01:13:56.059 --> 01:13:58.824
- Why didn't you tell me?
- [Clattering ]

01:13:58.892 --> 01:14:02.124
[Gasps]

01:14:03.826 --> 01:14:06.455
There's someone in the house.

01:14:06.525 --> 01:14:08.460
Get the hell outta here!

01:14:08.525 --> 01:14:11.927
- Oh. No, no, no, no, no.
- Jesus. What's going on?

01:14:11.992 --> 01:14:13.620
- Is he all right?
- Are you okay?

01:14:13.692 --> 01:14:16.355
- Who the fuck was that?
- Mike? Mike?

01:14:16.426 --> 01:14:19.362
Uh, does anybody know what to do?

01:14:19.426 --> 01:14:21.452
- Uh, Mike?
- Is he breathing?

01:14:21.525 --> 01:14:24.825
- Jesus Christ!
- Laurie, it's okay.

01:14:24.892 --> 01:14:26.383
[Screaming ]

01:14:26.459 --> 01:14:28.655
- Calm down.
- Laurie, Laurie, stop.

01:14:28.725 --> 01:14:31.854
- Laurie, Jesus.
- [Screaming ]

01:14:31.926 --> 01:14:34.794
- Shh.
- Kevin, shut her the fuck up.

01:14:34.859 --> 01:14:36.487
- [Sobbing ]
- It's okay, Laurie.

01:14:36.559 --> 01:14:38.790
Just breathe.
You're all right. You're all right.

01:14:38.859 --> 01:14:42.261
- [Shushing ]
- Em. Em.

01:14:42.326 --> 01:14:44.295
Em, where are you going?

01:14:44.359 --> 01:14:46.624
[Sobbing Continues]

01:14:46.692 --> 01:14:50.459
- [ Hysterical Crying ]
- Just calm down. It's all right.

01:14:50.525 --> 01:14:54.087
- Get off me!
- Get a rag. Get a towel. Anything.

01:14:54.159 --> 01:14:55.991
- Here, here, here, here.
- Get it off!

01:14:56.059 --> 01:14:58.893
- Get it off! I can't fucking stand blood.
- Okay. It's off.

01:14:58.959 --> 01:15:00.518
It'll be all right. Just calm down.

01:15:52.959 --> 01:15:56.088
[ Hugh ]
Get the fuck away. Get the fuck away.

01:15:56.159 --> 01:15:57.855
You're scaring the shit out of everybody.

01:15:57.926 --> 01:15:59.724
[ All talking ]

01:15:59.792 --> 01:16:04.025
Who are you?
Who are you fucking people?

01:16:23.259 --> 01:16:25.228
- And you said-
- All you guys are crazy.

01:16:25.293 --> 01:16:27.626
You were always fucking crazy.

01:16:29.393 --> 01:16:30.884
She's bad news.

01:16:30.959 --> 01:16:33.155
It's been years
we haven't seen each other.

01:16:57.692 --> 01:17:00.628
[Chattering, Laughing ]

01:17:08.826 --> 01:17:11.728
You know,
Vietnamese is a pitch-based language.

01:17:11.792 --> 01:17:15.285
D.H.R. Yeah.

01:17:15.359 --> 01:17:17.726
[Chatter, Laughter Continue]

01:17:17.792 --> 01:17:21.229
It really is a pitch-based language.

01:17:23.293 --> 01:17:26.229
- Hi.
- Hi.

01:17:26.293 --> 01:17:27.784
Cheers.

01:17:53.126 --> 01:17:58.224
[ Muffled Conversation ]

01:18:01.059 --> 01:18:02.994
And I don't think I'm working a lot.

01:18:03.059 --> 01:18:08.054
I have to work a lot,
but it's gonna be a nice balance.

01:18:08.126 --> 01:18:12.063
What are you gonna do while he's working?
What are you gonna do?

01:18:12.126 --> 01:18:13.788
I don't know. Just hang out.

01:18:13.859 --> 01:18:15.350
- Investigate?
- Yeah, investigate.

01:18:15.426 --> 01:18:17.691
Fundraise.
Get those Vietnamese to invest in-

01:18:17.759 --> 01:18:21.787
- Fundraise in San Francisco.
- Invest in the Vietnamese.

01:18:21.859 --> 01:18:24.829
- It's supposed to be gorgeous, though.
- This time of year.

01:18:24.892 --> 01:18:27.020
My cousin lived over there for about a year...

01:18:27.092 --> 01:18:28.583
and said it was just spectacular.

01:18:28.659 --> 01:18:32.994
- Have you been there before?
- No. Not Vietnam. Cambodia.

01:18:33.059 --> 01:18:34.550
Cambodia was awesome.

01:18:34.625 --> 01:18:36.526
Did you see Angkor Wat
when you were in Cambodia?

01:18:36.592 --> 01:18:38.083
- Yeah.
- Good times.

01:18:38.159 --> 01:18:39.718
[ Hinges Squeak]

01:18:41.393 --> 01:18:42.986
- [ Laughing ]
- Great.

01:18:43.059 --> 01:18:44.755
[ Laughter Continues]

01:18:44.826 --> 01:18:47.022
- Picture this.
- [Glass Shattering ]

01:18:47.092 --> 01:18:48.993
- Whoa. What the hell was that?
- What was that?

01:18:49.059 --> 01:18:51.585
- It was like a car window, or something.
- It sounded like glass.

01:18:51.659 --> 01:18:53.389
It sounded like a windshield.

01:18:53.459 --> 01:18:54.984
That's mine. That's mine.

01:18:55.059 --> 01:18:57.119
Should we get the, uh, the
glow sticks to take outside?

01:18:57.193 --> 01:18:58.684
We're not going to a rave.

01:18:58.759 --> 01:19:01.524
You want to go to a rave, party man?

01:19:01.592 --> 01:19:03.652
- Huh?
- I don't see anybody.

01:19:03.725 --> 01:19:05.591
You okay?

01:19:05.659 --> 01:19:09.061
- Whose is that right there?
- Oh, for fuck's sake. Seriously?

01:19:09.126 --> 01:19:12.790
- Oh, shit.
- Oh, baby.

01:19:12.859 --> 01:19:15.988
- I just got this. I just got this.
- I'm sorry.

01:19:16.059 --> 01:19:18.688
There's no structural damage.

01:19:18.759 --> 01:19:21.354
- Did they take anything?
- They didn't take my fucking-

01:19:21.426 --> 01:19:23.452
- They didn't take my stereo.
- Come on.

01:19:23.525 --> 01:19:26.654
- [Clears Throat ]
- Why don't we check the rest of our cars...

01:19:26.725 --> 01:19:28.216
and see what's going on.

01:19:28.293 --> 01:19:29.784
- Yeah.
- Honey, where's our car?

01:19:29.859 --> 01:19:31.851
- In the driveway.
- All right.

01:19:31.926 --> 01:19:35.522
- Em, you good?
- Yeah. I'm right up here.

01:19:37.725 --> 01:19:39.421
[Car Chirps Twice]

01:19:51.759 --> 01:19:54.786
[Gasping ]

01:19:58.826 --> 01:20:01.193
[ Panting ]

01:20:17.159 --> 01:20:19.025
[ Door Opening, Hinges Squeak]

01:20:19.092 --> 01:20:21.323
- Hey.
- Hey.

01:20:21.393 --> 01:20:23.885
What are you doing? We-Guys, she's in here.

01:20:23.959 --> 01:20:25.518
We were looking for you.

01:20:25.592 --> 01:20:29.029
- Oh, I was just, um, by my car.
- Oh.

01:20:29.092 --> 01:20:33.223
- You okay, babe?
- Yeah, I just-Yeah.

01:20:33.293 --> 01:20:35.762
- You got away from us.
- I did.

01:20:35.826 --> 01:20:38.694
I guess worse things could
happen at a dinner party.

01:20:38.759 --> 01:20:40.625
I went and got the-the ring.

01:20:40.692 --> 01:20:44.060
No, I could stay here. That's a good idea.

01:20:44.126 --> 01:20:46.391
What were you doing out there?

01:20:46.459 --> 01:20:50.294
Em. What were you doing out there?

01:20:50.359 --> 01:20:53.591
Um, the view is really beautiful
of the comet out there.

01:20:53.659 --> 01:20:56.094
- Oh.
- You came in that door?

01:20:56.159 --> 01:20:58.822
- Yeah.
- What's wrong with that door?

01:20:58.892 --> 01:21:02.124
That's the door to nowhere.
Don't you know?

01:21:02.193 --> 01:21:04.185
Okay. Let's go take a look.
Let's check it out.

01:21:04.259 --> 01:21:08.162
- Everybody's sick of hearing
about the feng shui.
- [Chattering ]

01:21:08.226 --> 01:21:11.287
- God, it's freezing outside.
- Come on.

01:21:11.359 --> 01:21:13.851
You mentioned it. Let's look at it.

01:21:13.926 --> 01:21:15.861
How come we never use this patio?

01:21:15.926 --> 01:21:17.656
Well, we never have comets.

01:21:17.725 --> 01:21:20.820
Oh, my God.

01:21:20.892 --> 01:21:22.554
W-What's it doing?

01:21:22.625 --> 01:21:24.719
It's breaking up.

01:21:24.792 --> 01:21:26.886
- Is that what they do?
- Yeah, I guess so.

01:21:26.959 --> 01:21:30.293
So, Em, is Katherine Meriss gonna understudy
your life while you're gone for a month?

01:21:30.359 --> 01:21:32.157
Oh, no one can. Ooh.

01:21:32.226 --> 01:21:33.717
[ Oohing ]

01:21:33.792 --> 01:21:36.728
- I like that.
- Oh, come on.

01:21:36.792 --> 01:21:38.886
[ All Chuckling ]

01:21:40.459 --> 01:21:42.485
I wish we could roast
marshmallows on that meteor.

01:21:42.559 --> 01:21:45.051
- [ All Chuckling ]
- A long stick.

01:22:08.592 --> 01:22:10.925
[Grunts]

01:22:15.393 --> 01:22:16.952
[Grunts]

01:22:34.059 --> 01:22:35.789
- [ Knock At Door]
- Yeah?

01:22:35.859 --> 01:22:37.851
- Em? You okay?
- Yeah?

01:22:37.926 --> 01:22:40.395
Yeah, I'm fine. The toilet just got backed up.

01:22:40.459 --> 01:22:43.327
You can't use that one.
You gotta use the main one, okay?

01:22:43.393 --> 01:22:45.658
Okay. I'll be right out.

01:23:17.959 --> 01:23:20.121
[ Door Opens, Shuts, Hinges Squeak]

01:23:22.525 --> 01:23:25.962
[Chattering ]

01:23:29.959 --> 01:23:32.121
- Oh, my God.
- Em. Em.

01:23:38.525 --> 01:23:40.926
[Sighs]

01:24:23.525 --> 01:24:26.290
Hey. You're up.

01:24:26.359 --> 01:24:29.261
I'll make some breakfast.
It'll be ready in, like, five minutes.

01:24:41.992 --> 01:24:44.461
[ Rattling ]

01:24:50.859 --> 01:24:53.260
Oh, hi. You feeling better?

01:24:53.326 --> 01:24:55.295
- Yeah.
- Okay.

01:24:55.359 --> 01:24:57.419
I'm gonna get dressed. I'll be back.

01:25:05.293 --> 01:25:07.592
[ Hinges Squeak]

01:25:30.992 --> 01:25:34.224
[ Kevin ]
Morning.

01:25:34.293 --> 01:25:36.421
You okay, babe?

01:25:36.492 --> 01:25:39.291
Are you okay?

01:25:39.359 --> 01:25:41.954
You totally passed out last night.

01:25:43.959 --> 01:25:47.623
You were mumbling. I put you on the couch.

01:25:47.692 --> 01:25:49.718
Found that in the bathroom.

01:25:51.992 --> 01:25:55.258
[ Phone Ringing ]

01:25:57.393 --> 01:26:00.955
That's weird. It's you calling me.

01:26:02.426 --> 01:26:04.418
Hello?

01:26:04.492 --> 01:26:08.327
[ Birds Twittering ]

